DESC:RADARLOCKSPECIALPOWER
	"Makes missiles hit faster and harder, though the launcher takes longer to get a target lock."
End

DESC:RADARLOCKSPECIALPOWEROFF
	"Reverts back to the standard missile config, which offers faster target locking."
End

DESC:RANDOMCRATE
	"One can only guess what wonders lie inside this securely-sealed supply container."
End

DESC:RAPIDLAUNCHSPECIALPOWER
	"Pushes rocket launchers past safety limits for faster firing--and internal damage."
End

DESC:RAPIDLAUNCHSPECIALPOWEROFF
	"Gives up the faster rate of fire to stop internal meltdowns from causing further damage."
End

DESC:RedAlertButton
	"In case of emergency, left-click button!\n» Grants up to 50,000 credits from your stash.\n» Grants heroic veterancy to all available forces.\n» Note: Challenge completion time will be void."
End

DESC:REPAIRMODE
	"Spend credits to repair damaged structures.\n\nLeft-click icon then left-click on target structure."
End

DESC:REPAIRMODECONSOLE
	"Initiate repairs on designated structures, which costs credits over time."
End

DESC:REVERSEMOVE
	"Selected vehicles will move backwards to target location, if they can--useful for some defensive tactics.\n\nLeft-click icon then right-click on target location."
End

DESC:ROARSPECIALPOWER
	"Paralyzes nearby enemy infantry with a deafening war cry. Also tenderizes meat."
End

DESC:RUSHMOREFIRINGBASE
	"Suffice it to say, this structure must be destroyed before the President's limo arrives."
End

DESC:RUSHMOREHEADCONTROLCENTER_JEFFERSON
	"Capture this facility with an Engineer to deactivate the bust of Jefferson."
End

DESC:RushmoreHeadControlCenter_Lincoln
	"Capture this facility with an Engineer to deactivate the bust of Abe Lincoln."
End

DESC:RushmoreHeadControlCenter_Washington
	"Capture this facility with an Engineer to deactivate the bust of Washington."
End

DESC:RUSHMORERADARTOWER
	"This antenna enables remote access to the defensive network here at Mt. Rushmore."
End

DESC:S08SpecialCarrier
	"The emissary aboard this carrier naïvely volunteered to treat with the Premier's men."
End

DESC:S08SpecialDreadnought
	"The ambassador aboard this ship has confidential orders directly from the Premier."
End

DESC:SA_BESTBUY
	"Capture this unassuming retail store with an Engineer for a steady influx of credits!"
End

DESC:SA_GAME
	"Capture this unassuming retail store with an Engineer for a steady influx of credits!"
End

DESC:SA_GAMESTOP
	"Capture this unassuming retail store with an Engineer for a steady influx of credits!"
End

DESC:SA_OBSERVATORYDEFENSIVEGUN
	"Devastating long-range artillery by day, observatory by night. Approach with caution."
End

DESC:SANTAMONICAPIER
	"Civilians used these contraptions to leave their worries behind before the war came."
End

DESC:SATELLITELAUNCHFACILITY
	"Reactivating this old satellite launch facility should bring orbital defenses back online."
End

DESC:SELLMODE
	"Sell a structure for an instant refund based on the structure's condition.\n\nLeft-click icon then left-click on target structure."
End

DESC:SELLMODECONSOLE
	"Sell designated structures for an instant refund in credits."
End

DESC:ShinzoHouse
	"The Nagama clan's ancestral residence must be frozen in order for its master to be subdued."
End

DESC:SHIPYARDTECHSTRUCTURE
	"Capture this structure with an Engineer and all your navy units will automatically self-repair!"
End

DESC:SHROUDCRATE
	"Order a unit onto this unassuming device to suddenly reveal the surrounding area."
End

DESC:SMOKEBOMBSPECIALPOWER
	"Vanishes in a puff of smoke, causing enemy assailants to lose their target in bewilderment."
End

DESC:SOVIETAIRFIELD
	"As Soviet air power grew, these facilities became necessary for maintaining various aircraft."
End

DESC:SOVIETAIRFIELDRETURNTOBASE
	"Orders any aircraft that were docked at this Airfield to return to base immediately."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTIAIRSHIP
	"All-terrain transports boasting highly-effective AA guns and unorthodox ejection systems."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTIGROUNDAIRCRAFT
	"Combat helicopters armed to the teeth with guns and rockets. Can haul troops or vehicles."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTIINFANTRYINFANTRY
	"Young frontliners armed with assault rifles, promises of glory, and explosive cocktails."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTIINFANTRYVEHICLE
	"Rickety mechanical walkers that can engage multiple hostiles with their triple machine guns."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTINAVYSHIPTECH1
	"Insulated, lightly armored vessels armed with electrifying Tesla weapons. Can clamber ashore."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTINAVYSHIPTECH2
	"Hidden killers that surface only to fire. Nothing can withstand their torpedoes for long."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTISTRUCTURESHIP
	"The big brothers of the Red Navy, these massive siege ships host an array of V4 rockets."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTISTRUCTUREVEHICLE
	"Mobile long-range ballistic-rocket platforms that can level a city block with one launch."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTIVEHICLEINFANTRY
	"Burly convicts forced to carry heavy anti-air flak cannons and satchels of volatile mines."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTIVEHICLEVEHICLETECH1
	"Sturdy main battle tanks that symbolize the Red Army. Can siphon armor from their enemies."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTIVEHICLEVEHICLETECH2
	"Heavily-armored behemoths fitted with a pair of Tesla Coils, which can slag vehicles in a flash."
End

DESC:SOVIETANTIVEHICLEVEHICLETECH3
	"Monstrous self-repairing tanks that can run over anything their ferocious cannons let live."
End

DESC:SOVIETBARRACKS
	"All Soviet infantry are trained, sometimes hastily, at modest facilities such as this."
End

DESC:SOVIETBASEDEFENSEADVANCED
	"Ominous, lightning-shooting towers. May be powered by Tesla Troopers or Stingrays."
End

DESC:SOVIETBASEDEFENSEAIR
	"Rapid-fire air defense cannons that fill the skies with a hailstorm of metal shards."
End

DESC:SOVIETBASEDEFENSEGROUND
	"Heavy machine gun nests manned by Soviet conscripts relegated to guard duty."
End

DESC:SOVIETBOMBERAIRCRAFT
	"Fearsome war-zeppelins boasting self-sealing armor and vast stores of heavy iron bombs."
End

DESC:SOVIETBOMBERAIRCRAFT_SPECIAL
	"A Kirov armed with but one gargantuan bomb, intended for an unsuspecting Allied city."
End

DESC:SOVIETBUNKER
	"Infantry may shoot from out of this makeshift bunker, which affords them some protection."
End

DESC:SovietChiefEngineer
	"Anonymous donors of new Soviet weapons technology, once to the Soviets and now the Allies."
End

DESC:SOVIETCOMMANDOTECH1
	"Spitting image of a ruthless, legendary markswoman. Authorized to call airstrikes."
End

DESC:SOVIETCONSTRUCTIONYARD
	"Heart of any Soviet base. They assemble military structures and may pack up into MCVs."
End

DESC:SOVIETCRANE
	"Industrial cranes used to construct structures and repair vehicles--or scrap them for cash."
End

DESC:SovietDesolatorInfantry
	"Thick chemical suits shield these sadists from the horrid poisons they use as weapons."
End

DESC:SOVIETENGINEER
	"Grizzled, pistol-packing men of science who can capture or repair structures."
End

DESC:SOVIETFIGHTERAIRCRAFT
	"Sleek and elusive jetfighters that can pulverize enemy squadrons with their burst-missiles."
End

DESC:SOVIETFIGHTERAIRCRAFTRETURNTOAIRFIELD
	"Causes the MiG Fighter to immediately turn tail and double back to an Airfield to rearm."
End

DESC:SovietGrinderVehicle
	"Road rollers jury-rigged for war. Their gnashing teeth can grind anything on land or sea."
End

DESC:SOVIETHEAVYANTIVEHICLEINFANTRY
	"Heavily-armored, lightning-shooting bruisers who can go toe-to-toe with enemy tanks."
End

DESC:SovietHeavyWalkerDeployedTurret
	"Legless and entrenched, these failed prototypes still can deal death to whatever draws near."
End

DESC:SovietHeavyWalkerVehicle
	"Bigger, tougher relatives of the Sickle that can barely lift all their rockets and grenades."
End

DESC:SovietLargeScoutInfantry
	"Genetically-mutated War Bears created to cause even bigger problems for the Union's enemies."
End

DESC:SOVIETMCV
	"Heavily-armored, self-powered production vehicles used to push the front lines."
End

DESC:SOVIETMINER
	"Simple armored vehicles that gather raw resources with which to fuel the Soviet War Machine."
End

DESC:SovietMortarCycle
	"These souped-up bikes would be even faster if not for all the explosives they carry."
End

DESC:SOVIETNAVALYARD
	"These structures are authorized to build and maintain any class of vessel in the Soviet navy."
End

DESC:SOVIETOUTPOST
	"The Soviets tend to expand their sprawling bases around these operations hubs."
End

DESC:SOVIETPOWERPLANT
	"Soviet facilities and base defenses require considerable power, which Reactors provide."
End

DESC:SOVIETPOWERPLANTADVANCED
	"Symbolic of Soviet excesses, these dangerously volatile structures could fuel a city."
End

DESC:SOVIETRADARDISH
	"Radar Dishes enables the tactical minimap feature of the Battlefield Control interface."
End

DESC:SOVIETREFINERY
	"Ore Collectors toil between these and ore gathering points, filling Soviet coffers."
End

DESC:SOVIETSCOUTINFANTRY
	"Savage beasts trained in close-quarters combat and recon. Enemy disguises can't trick them."
End

DESC:SOVIETSCOUTVEHICLE
	"Unsettling little combat robots that can bore into flesh or metal. Waterproof up to 100 meters."
End

DESC:SovietStatue
	"People of the Union pay their respects to such lifeless idols, rather than to the Empire."
End

DESC:SOVIETSUPERWEAPON
	"Emits a strange kinetic barrier that makes targets invulnerable, briefly. Lethal to infantry."
End

DESC:SOVIETSUPERWEAPONADVANCED
	"Soviet scientists laughed aside ethical concerns while inventing this monstrous warhead."
End

DESC:SOVIETSURVEYOR
	"Smaller and humbler than MCVs, these unarmed vehicles can set up expansion bases."
End

DESC:SOVIETTECHSTRUCTURE
	"These unlock the latest weapons while silently analyzing combat data for future use."
End

DESC:SOVIETVIPBUNKER
	"A high-ranking Soviet commander is inside this facility, personally supervising the mission."
End

DESC:SOVIETWALLPIECE
	"Two wall pieces placed in an unbroken row will form a thick barrier that blocks enemies."
End

DESC:SOVIETWARFACTORY
	"The infamous Soviet tank divisions and other vehicles are built from these facilities."
End

DESC:ST_LENINGRADMISSLEBASE
	"From a tactical point of view, whatever this is, it can be destroyed if it gets in the way."
End

DESC:ST_LENINGRADMISSLEBASE_01
	"Not only is this museum educational, it contains rocket launchers. An Engineer could operate them."
End

DESC:ST_SHUTTLEBUILDING
	"A symbol of the Soviet Union, this proud fortress houses countless cultural treasures."
End

DESC:STOP
	"Selected units will cease performing any command they were given and resume acting based on their stance.\n\nLeft-click icon to stop units."
End

DESC:SUPERTORPEDOSSPECIALPOWER
	"Launches a pair of unguided high-yield torpedoes to smash into anything dead ahead."
End

DESC:SUPPORTQUEUECONSOLE
	"Manage all Support Structure build queues, for making base defenses, walls, and superweapons."
End

DESC:SUPPORTSTRUCTURESUBTAB
	"Manage individual Support Structure build queues."
End

DESC:SUPPORTSTRUCTURETAB
	"Manage all Support Structure build queues."
End

DESC:TECHBUILDINGOILDERRICK
	"Capture this structure with an Engineer and it will provide you with a steady flow of income!"
End

DESC:TECHBUILDINGORENODE
	"Provides precious raw materials suitable for military funding on a first-come, first-served basis."
End

DESC:TECHBUILDINGORENODE2
	"Provides raw materials suitable for efficient military production. Room enough for two Collectors!"
End

DESC:TECHBUILDINGORENODE4
	"Provides raw materials suitable for efficient military production. Room enough for four Collectors!"
End

DESC:TECHBUILDINGPOWERPLANT
	"Capture this structure with an Engineer and enjoy the boost to your base's energy reserves. Smooth!"
End

DESC:TECHSTORETAB
	"Spend Security Points earned in battle on a variety of useful military maneuvers!"
End

DESC:TESLANOVASPECIALPOWER
	"Jolts surrounding waters with intense electrical current, briefly disabling the Stingray."
End

DESC:TH_JapanHiveGenerator
	"The Rising Sun's enhanced shield generator can sustain an impenetrable barrier indefinitely."
End

DESC:THREATMETER
	"A highly-scientific measure of chaos and destruction over time.\n\nThe higher the Threat Level, the faster you earn Security Points and your units gain veterancy."
End

DESC:TIMEBELTSPECIALPOWER
	"Snaps Tanya back several moments in time ago using her one-of-a-kind belt buckle."
End

DESC:TOGGLEAFTERBURNERS
	"Yields more-respectable top speeds as unstable chemicals eat away at overall hull integrity."
End

DESC:TOGGLEAFTERBURNERSOFF
	"Reverts to standard slow-and-ominous speed and stops taking damage from chemical burn."
End

desc:togglealliedartiddsslleryautocannon
	"Plants the Pacifier into the ground so that it can use its long-range cannon."
End

desc:togglealliedartilleryautocannon
	"Detaches from the ground, retracts the Grand Cannon, and readies two 7.62 mm miniguns."
End

desc:togglealliedartillerysiegeweapon
	"Fastens firmly into the ground in order to use the Grand Cannon long-range artillery."
End

desc:togglealliedgunship
	"Switches to a 25 mm anti-personnel weapon that can chew through infantry in droves."
End

desc:togglealliedgunshipautocannon
	"Re-enables the vaunted Collider Cannons, which pack the punch of the Allies' ultimate weapon."
End

DESC:TOGGLEARMORUP
	"Deploys special ceramic armor, which also reduces speed and covers the cargo hold."
End

DESC:TOGGLEARMORUPOFF
	"Folds up the anti-tank armor, regaining mobility and the ability to carry out ore gathering."
End

DESC:TOGGLEBINARYWEAPON
	"Switches from its primary attack mode to an immobilizing ray that stops enemy vehicles."
End

DESC:TOGGLEBINARYWEAPONOFF
	"Switches to the dismantler claws, which can bore into enemy combatants."
End

DESC:TOGGLELEECHBEAM
	"Switches to using the Leech-Beam, which siphons armor and weapons from target vehicles."
End

DESC:TOGGLELEECHBEAMOFF
	"Switches to the 85 mm autoloading cannon, along with any leeched secondary weapon."
End

DESC:TOGGLELOCKDOWNGUNSPECIALPOWER
	"Switches from photon rockets to the Paralysis Whip, which locks down surface units."
End

DESC:TOGGLELOCKDOWNGUNSPECIALPOWEROFF
	"Switches to the photon rocket array, which overwhelms targets with countless warheads."
End

DESC:TOGGLERIOTSHIELDUPGRADE
	"Switches to using a bulletproof shield, which can make it easier to get up nice and close."
End

DESC:TOGGLERIOTSHIELDUPGRADEOFF
	"Switches to the Grummond-8 pump shotgun, which is effective in close-quarters combat."
End

DESC:TOGGLESHIELDSPHERE
	"Generates an emergency energy barrier to temporarily repel incoming fire."
End

DESC:ToggleSovietMortarcycleMolotov
	"Packs up the Mortar so the sidecar gunner can resume dishing out explosive cocktails."
End

DESC:ToggleSovietMortarcycleMortar
	"Unpacks a light artillery piece for use against medium-to-long-range targets."
End

DESC:TOGGLESPIDERHOLE
	"Escapes into a spider hole for increased protection and to avoid being crushed."
End

DESC:TOGGLESPIDERHOLEOFF
	"Backs out of the spider hole to resume fighting like a man. Regain honor when possible."
End

DESC:TORPEDOSPREADSPECIALPOWER
	"Launches a fanlike spread of ship-killing warheads, held in concealed secondary launchers."
End

DESC:UNITCRATE
	"A crate that spawns a unit when collected."
End

DESC:UNITINTRO
	"Watch a quick video showing off the selected unit's primary and special abilities."
End

DESC:UNITSMENUTAB
	"Manage your currently selected units or structure."
End

DESC:VARIABLEWEAPONTRANSFORMOFF2
	"Switch to anti-surface configuration and heavily deter enemy infantry by means of death."
End

DESC:VEHICLEGROUP
	"Select all vehicles in the field."
End

DESC:VEHICLEQUEUECONSOLE
	"Manage all ground-based Vehicle build queues."
End

DESC:VEHICLESUBTAB
	"Manage individual Vehicle production structures."
End

DESC:VEHICLETAB
	"Manage all Vehicle build queues."
End

DESC:VETERANCYCRATE
	"Order a unit to get this helpful, conveniently-situated device to raise its experience level."
End

DESC:VETERANCYTECHSTRUCTURE
	"Capture this structure with an Engineer and all your units will start with veteran rank!"
End

DESC:VOICECHATMODE
	"Chatting to Allies vs. Chatting to All"
End

DESC:VOICECHATMODEALL
	"Currently chatting to all Players"
End

DESC:VOICECHATMODEALLIES
	"Currently chatting to only Allies"
End

DESC:VOICECHATMODESPECIFIC
	"This icon indicates you are currently broadcasting your voice stream to other players"
End

DESC:VOLCANOFORTRESS
	"The scheming and paranoid Premier Cherdenko is holed up inside this diabolical fortress."
End

DESC:WAYPOINTMODE
	"Use Waypoint Mode to give sequential commands to the selected units--useful for prioritizing enemy targets.\n\nLeft-click icon then issue a sequence of commands."
End

DESC:WEAPONSCRAMBLESPECIALPOWER
	"Switches to using the Scramblegun weapon jammer, which stops targets from firing."
End

DESC:WEAPONSCRAMBLESPECIALPOWEROFF
	"Swaps out the Weapon Jammer for the Icarus 20 mm CIWS anti-aircraft cannon."
End

DESC:YURIKO_POWERS_MENU
	"Unlock the secrets of Yuriko's latent psionic powers in this handy menu! Limit one latent psionic power per each Secret File discovered during Yuriko's journey."
End

DESCRIPTION:BUTTONJAIV_TRANSFORM
	"Switches to Jet Tengu flight configuration for air superiority and superior mobility."
End

DESCRIPTION:BUTTONJAIV_TRANSFORMOFF
	"Switches to amphibious Mecha Tengu mode for anti-infantry fast-attack capability."
End

DESCRIPTION:SPECIALPOWERSHRINKRAY
	"Zaps ground units down to an embarrassing and easily crushable yet speedy little size."
End

DESCRIPTION:UPGRADEALLIEDTECH2
	"Receive encrypted signals that unlock the next tier of units at your production structures."
End

DESCRIPTION:UPGRADEALLIEDTECH3
	"The full brunt of the Allied military becomes available once these permissions are granted."
End

DESCRIPTION:UPGRADEJAPANBARRACKSTECH2
	"Expands this facility to the next level, granting access to recruit Imperial Shinobi."
End

DESCRIPTION:UPGRADEJAPANBARRACKSTECH3
	"Completes the expansion of this facility, enabling access to Japan's elite women warriors."
End

DESCRIPTION:UPGRADEJAPANCONSTRUCTIONYARDTECH2
	"Expands this facility to the next level, unlocking new technology for production."
End

DESCRIPTION:UPGRADEJAPANCONSTRUCTIONYARDTECH3
	"Completes the expansion of this facility, unlocking additional production options."
End

DESCRIPTION:UPGRADEJAPANNAVALYARDTECH2
	"Expands this facility to the next level, unlocking a wider variety of units for production."
End

DESCRIPTION:UPGRADEJAPANNAVALYARDTECH3
	"Completes the expansion of this facility, allowing the mighty Shogun Battleship to be built."
End

DESCRIPTION:UPGRADEJAPANWARFACTORYTECH2
	"Expands this facility to the next level, unlocking new vehicles for production."
End

DESCRIPTION:UPGRADEJAPANWARFACTORYTECH3
	"Completes the expansion of this facility, unlocking the latest mechanized forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL41
	"Hold your fire against Shinzo's palace.[2.1]He must be subdued."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL42
	"Cease the assault on Shinzo's transport.[2.3]He must be subdued."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL43
	"Do not attack Shinzo! He must be subdued."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL44
	"This is our only Construction Vehicle in the area.[2.6]It must be defended."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL45
	"Escort this Mobile Construction Vehicle to the designated location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL46
	"Eliminate Shinzo's defenses."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL47
	"Use cryo weapons to freeze and subdue Shinzo."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL48
	"With the aid of Tatsu, we are deploying forces to the Iga Province, the ancestral homeland of the Nagama family.  "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL49
	"Shinzo must be subdued using our cryo-technology, for safe transport to our military detention centre."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL50
	"You will need to escort a Mobile Construction Vehicle to the designated location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL51
	"Defeat Shinzo's fief-dom forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL52
	"And finally freeze Shinzo."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL53
	"Harbinger Gunships en route to your location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL54
	"These Gunships can lay down heavy suppressive fire over an area and are armed with a variety of powerful weapons.[5.7]Use them with care."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL55
	"The warlord Shinzo Nagama is holding out at his clan's village. Your mission is to subdue him so he can be brought to justice. Specifically:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL56
	"Establish a forward base in the vicinity of Shinzo's main base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL57
	"Defeat Shinzo's loyalist forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL58
	"Use our cryo technology to capture Shinzo alive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL59
	"Because the war with the Empire of the Rising Sun is officially over, we cannot commit our full arsenal in this operation. We appreciate your flexibility. Godspeed Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL60
	"Shinzo Nagama has been killed[2.1]-- the purpose of this operation was to subdue him.[4.6]Aborting mission."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL61
	"Your forces were defeated and Allied Command cannot commit additional reinforcements.[4.6]Mission aborted."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDINTEL62
	"Imperial anti-air power here is greater than expected.[3.1]Commander, beware of the Archer Maiden division serving Commander Shinzo. Their bows are uncommonly dangerous."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDSOLDIER07
	"Don't leave us behind, sir!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDSOLDIER08
	"Imperial Forces Incoming![1.7]Get in those buildings!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDSOLDIER09
	"Wait…who controls these Dojos?[2.1]Tatsu or us?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_ALLIEDSOLDIER10
	"I wish we had more ladies in -our- infantry divisions… heh heh heh."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_IMPERIALSOLDIER01
	"Invaders! Sound the alarms!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_IMPERIALSOLDIER02
	"Barbarians? Here?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_IMPERIALSOLDIER03
	"How dare you desecrate our sacred land!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA01_IMPERIALSOLDIER04
	"Lets go get them! Move out!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL35
	"The Nanoswarm barriers here are an improved design, and will not dissipate on their own.[4.7]You will need to find a way to bring them down."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL36
	"Power has been cut to one of the Nanoswarm barriers.[2.5]Strike now while there is time."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL37
	"The Nanoswarm barrier protecting Kenji's estate has been deactivated.[3.4]Muster force and destroy the estate to flush Kenji out."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL38
	"Kenji has activated a Tech Inhibitor.[2.5]You are authorized to destroy it to ensure mission success."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL39
	"We no longer have the forces to bring down the defenses.[3]Aborting mission."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL40
	"The Imperial forces are too strong!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL41
	"You have failed to bring down the Tech Inhibitor.[2.4]Mission aborted."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL42
	"Warlord Kenji has been subdued and will be transported to our detention center in the vicinity.[5]Mission accomplished."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL43
	"With the Nanoswarm barriers down, we have an opportunity to marshal more forces.[4.1]Establish a base before Kenji's loyalists can regain their footing."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL44
	"Kenji's estate has been destroyed. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL45
	"Prepare to close in on Kenji's location -- priority overridden.[3.8]Caution. We detect that one of our own Tech Inhibitors has been activated and is being used against us."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL46
	"Use caution inside the city, Commander.[2.3]Resistance forces may have occupied the civilian structures here."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL47
	"Tatsu has requested help in repairing the bridge leading to his forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL48
	"Tatsu would be grateful if we were to capture the Imperial Mecha Bays and Instant Dojos in the area. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL49
	"The Tech Inhibitor prevents us from capturing Kenji.[2.7]You will need to use infantry forces to destroy it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL50
	"The former Shogunate commander Kenji Tenzai has been tracked to his well-fortified headquarters in Osaka. Your mission is to bring him in, alive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL51
	"Find a way to neutralize the Nanoswarm defenses barring passage to Kenji's headquarters."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL52
	"Find a way to neutralize the Nanoswarm defenses barring passage to Kenji's villa. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL53
	"Find a way to flush Kenji out of hiding."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL54
	"Once he is pinpointed, we will use our Chronosphere network to detain him."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL55
	"Expect heavy resistance from forces honor-bound to the rogue commander. Good luck, Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL56
	"Kenji has been killed in action.[1.8]Your task was to capture him alive. Mission failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL57
	"Your forces have been destroyed.[1.7]Kenji is left to flee and continue sowing the seeds of revolution.[5]Mission aborted."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL58
	"A squad of Cryo Legionnaires has arrived to assist in the capture operation.[3.7]Their ice beams can stop enemy combatants cold."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL59
	"You may train additional Cryo Legionnaires from your Boot Camp."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL60
	"Tech Inhibitor destroyed.[1.7]Chronosphere network connection re-established.[3.9]Preparing to use the Chronosphere on Kenji's location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDINTEL61
	"Kenji's estate is defended by anti-tank robots called the Steel Ronin.[3.8]Our armor divisions are advised to avoid engaging them directly."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDSOLDIER03
	"The fortress is protected by the Nanoswarm Generators!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDSOLDIER04
	"I bet one of them Cryo Legionnaires could deal with all those guys."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA02_ALLIEDSOLDIER05
	"Who takes control of the army if all of the shogun are dead?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL20
	"Transport your construction vehicle to one of the indicated deployment zones as soon as possible.[4.4]Proceed with caution."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL21
	"Your MCV is under attack- It must be defended."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL22
	"The enemy knows you are here and are preparing assault forces.[2.8]Muster your defenses as soon as possible."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL23
	"Takara is entrenched in the area to the north.[2.6]She must be defeated to end this conflict."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL24
	"Takara is attempting to wall in your Construction Yard.[2.7]Prevent those nanocores from unfurling or retreat from them if necessary."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL25
	"Enemy flight group detected. It is recommended that you prepare anti-air defenses.[4.2]Takara may attack from any direction."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL26
	"Tatsu has taken up arms against us once again, and our negotations were for naught.[4.5]Allied Command asks that you end this destructive conflict once and for all."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL27
	"Commander, Tatsu has stolen access to the Chronosphere network."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL28
	"Be advised, Commander: It appears Tatsu is using our Chronosphere against us."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL29
	"Tatsu is transporting his naval forces into range of our base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL30
	"Tatsu has found a way to use the Chronosphere on his base structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL31
	"Commander--Tatsu has somehow transported his entire base to another position!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL32
	"Chronosphere signatures detected.[1.6]Commander, prevent Tatsu from transporting his base again. There is no telling what he will do."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL33
	"Tatsu's forces have been stopped.[1.8]This mission is a success thanks to you, Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL34
	"The rebellious Imperial commander Takara is holed up with remnant forces near Miyako."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL35
	"She is to be neutralized. Tatsu and Allied Command expect that this will put a stop to the rebellion. Your mission is:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL36
	"Breach Takara's defensive perimeter with your Mobile Construction Vehicle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL37
	"Defeat Takara and her resistance forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL38
	"Expect forces sworn to Tatsu to support your final objective."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL39
	"This operation should finally quell the insurgency in the Empire of the Rising Sun. Take care and good luck."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL40
	"We have released our latest vehicle, the Pacifier FAV, for you to use against the entrenched enemy forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL41
	"Once deployed, the Pacifier's Grand Cannon can fire across great distances."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL42
	"Our suppliers at FutureTech have released several of their experimental FutureTank X-1s to aid your mission.[5.6]They are said to be the strongest Allied ground forces to date."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL43
	"Massive energy fluctuations detected.[2.3]Intel indicates that Tatsu has activated a new weapon called the Giga-Fortress.[6.5]Be on your guard, Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDINTEL44
	"Takara opposes Tatsu, who tricked us into attacking her.[3.2]In spite of the loss of her forces, she has united with us to stop Tatsu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDSOLDIER07
	"I knew we couldn't trust Tatsu![1.7]Oh, the hubris!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDSOLDIER08
	"You can't trust any of these Rising Sun dirtbags--they're way too proud."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MA03_ALLIEDSOLDIER09
	"If Tatsu unites the army, we're done for!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_AIRCRAFTCARRIER
	"Aircraft Carriers are powerful naval artillery platforms, which can neutralize enemy installations from a safe distance.[6.6]Their combat drones automatically return to rearm between bombing runs.[10.9]Carriers can also launch the Blackout Missile, which deactivates vehicles or structures caught in its blast."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_APOLLOFIGHTER
	"Apollo Fighters are air-superiority jets, armed with rapid-fire cannons that can tear enemy aircraft to bits.[6.1]Their special ability is to quickly return to their Airbase to reload and repair as necessary."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_ASSAULTDESTROYER
	"Assault Destroyers are sturdy amphibious warships armed with heavy cannons effective against armored targets.[6.2]Instead of using their main guns, they can activate their Black-Hole Armor, which automatically draws incoming fire directed at nearby friendly forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_ATHENACANNON
	"Athena Cannons are mobile artillery units linked to our space defense network.[4.2]They can pinpoint targets from long range, causing a proton beam to fire down from orbit.[9.1]Their special ability is the Aegis shield, a barrier that temporarily protects the Athena cannon and nearby units.[15.3]Athena Cannons cannot act while the shield is up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_ATTACKDOG
	"Attack Dogs are trained for amphibious scouting and light combat.[3.1]Their attack is lethal to most infantry.[5]They can detect disguised enemy units as well.[7.8]Their special ability is a deafening bark that paralyzes enemy infantry within earshot."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_CENTURYBOMBER
	"Century Bombers are well-armored flying infantry transports that can carpet-bomb enemy bases to dust.[5.5]They must rearm back at an Airbase between bombing runs, at which time they can pick up more infantry to paradrop behind enemy lines."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_CRYCOPTER
	"Cryocopters are special support units which can freeze targets.[3.3]Frozen units cannot act and are highly vulnerable to attack.[7.2]The Cryocopter's special ability is the Shrink Beam, which temporarily reduces a target in size, making it less powerful and easily crushed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_CRYOLEGIONNAIRE
	"Cryo Legionnaires are heavy assault infantry whose ice cannons can freeze multiple assailants dead in their tracks in just a few seconds.[7]The Cryo Legionnaires' special ability is the boost kick, which they use to shatter frozen targets, or leap into or out of battle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_DOLPHIN
	"The Allied navy employs specially-trained Dolphins armed with sonic weapons for scouting the seas and intercepting enemy ships.[6.9]Dolphins have the special ability to jump up and out of the water to avoid dangerous situations."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_ENGINEER
	"Though defenseless against enemy units, Engineers can capture neutral or enemy structures on land or at sea.[6.1]They can also repair your damaged structures.[8.8]Their special ability is to set up a first-aid tent, which causes any of your infantry units in the vicinity to gradually recover from injuries."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_FUTURETANK
	"FutureTank X-1s are heavily armored, computer-controlled combat vehicles that are virtually unmatched on the ground.[6.2]Their experimental cannons can easily cut through even the toughest armor, while their Riot Beam special weapon lets them turn the tables on enemies attacking in mass."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_GUARDIANTANK
	"Guardian Tanks are armed with main guns that work well against most vehicles and structures.[4.4]These tanks can even crush enemy infantry.[7.3]Their special ability is to switch to a targeting laser that reduces the armor of an enemy, making it more vulnerable to attack."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_HARBINGER
	"Harbinger Gunships are massive support aircraft armed with the latest in weapons technology.[5.1]Next to nothing can resist their on-board collider cannons, but just in case, they can switch to fast-firing antipersonnel guns for taking care of any smaller threats."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_HYDROFOIL
	"Hydrofoils are swift vessels that can quickly cut through enemy aircraft using their rapid-firing autocannons.[5.9]Their special ability is to switch to using a Weapon Jammer, which prevents targeted foes from attacking."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_JAVELINSOLDIER
	"Javelin Soldiers carry portable missile launchers effective against enemy armor and aircraft.[5.3]Their special ability is to switch to laser-guided mode, in which it takes longer to acquire a target, but grants a much faster firing rate."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_MCV
	"Mobile Construction Vehicles are amphibious mobile HQs.[3.7]Though unarmed, they are the focal point of Allied military operations.[7.6]They can unpack into Construction Yards, which build all Allied structures.[11.4]Do whatever it takes to protect these facilities."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_MIRAGETANK
	"Mirage Tanks automatically camouflage themselves as innocuous objects while immobile.[4.4]They can devastate surface targets with their spectrum cannons.[7.7]Their special ability is to switch on a device that makes nearby forces invisible to the enemy.[12.8]Mirage Tanks cannot camouflage or fire in this mode."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_MULTIGUNNERIFV
	"Multigunner IFVs are quick and versatile jack-of-all-trades vehicles that automatically switch weapons depending on which infantry unit is riding inside.[9.4]Their stock weapon is an anti-air/anti-surface rocket launcher, though they can be specialized to repair vehicles, counter enemy infantry, and more."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_PACIFIER
	"Pacifier Field Artillery Vehicles can neutralize enemy combatants from long range using their Grand Cannons.[5.9]They must deploy to a fixed position on land to initiate bombardment.[9.8]When not deployed, Pacifiers may cross land or sea and defend themselves with heavy machineguns."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_PEACEKEEPER
	"Peacekeepers are shotgun-wielding frontline infantry who can knock enemy infantry to the ground whilst in close quarters.[7]Their special ability is to switch to using a riot shield, which provides added defense whilst allowing them to close the distance with their foes."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_PROSPECTOR
	"Prospectors are amphibious resource-collecting vehicles.[3]They are unarmed and need to be protected.[5.7]Their special ability is to unpack into Command Hubs.[8.7]Other structures may then be built nearby.[11.1]This conversion is irreversible yet essential for expanding to new locations."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_RIPTIDE
	"Riptide ACVs are all-terrain assault transports, with room for several infantry as well as a mounted machine gun for protection.[7.3]Riptides are more powerful at sea, where they can attack using torpedos as well as their gun.[12.1]They are useful for rushing infantry behind enemy lines."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_SPY
	"While Spies are unarmed, they can disguise themselves as other infantry and attempt to sneak into enemy bases on land or sea.[6.8]Enemy scouts can break their disguise.[9.2]They can infiltrate structures, causing the enemy base to suffer various consequences.[14]Spies can also bribe enemy units near them to join your cause, for a fee."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_TANYA
	"Special Agent Tanya Adams is our finest commando.[2.7]She can easily dispatch enemy infantry with her pistols, and eliminate structures and vehicles with her explosives.[8.6]Tanya is a remarkable swimmer too.[10.6]Her special ability is the Time Belt, which instantly transports her back in time several moments and can get her out of harm's way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MAIN_VINDICATOR
	"Vindicators are close-support bombers effective against enemy vehicles.[3.8]They must reload at an Airbase between bombing runs.[7]They have a special ability that lets them quickly return to base to rearm and repair when needed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME01_SOVIETSOLDIER06
	"Our Grinders will turn your pathetic vehicles into dust!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME01_SOVIETSOLDIER07
	"They're retreating, push forward, push forward! OORAH!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME01_SOVIETSOLDIER08
	"What the...our own forces are attacking US?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME01_SOVIETSOLDIER09
	"Reinforcments en route for dropoff."
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME01_SOVIETSOLDIER10
	"With these reinforcements, the Empire stands no chance against us."
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME01_SOVIETSOLDIER11
	"Uh…why is one of our ships on land…?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME01_SOVIETSOLDIER12
	"There's something fishy about that one vehicle there, but I can't put my finger on it…"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME02_SOVIETSOLDIER01
	"Capture that Observation Post quickly!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME02_SOVIETSOLDIER02
	"Get our defenses up, now!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME02_SOVIETSOLDIER03
	"Destroy everything! Leave no building standing!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME02_SOVIETSOLDIER04
	"It's an ambush! "
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME02_SOVIETSOLDIER05
	"They're along the coast, take them out, now!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME02_SOVIETSOLDIER06
	"These islands will belong to Mother Russia!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME02_SOVIETSOLDIER07
	"Your precious shrine is destroyed! "
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME02_SOVIETSOLDIER08
	"The islands are ours! "
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME03_SOVIETSOLDIER09
	"This is Soviet land! How dare you set foot upon it!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME03_SOVIETSOLDIER10
	"They're flanking from the north!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME03_SOVIETSOLDIER11
	"Quickly, regroup to the northwestern expansion!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME03_SOVIETSOLDIER12
	"Hurry, they're right on top of us!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME03_SOVIETSOLDIER13
	"Whaa-- That thing's bigger than a Kirov!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:ME03_SOVIETSOLDIER14
	"Quickly, we need anti-air to take down that monstrosity!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL36
	"Our national defense force on Sakhalin Island is under attack by Soviet forces. Commander Kenji has requested immediate backup, which you will provide."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL37
	"Due to the Allied occupation of our country, our best option is to sneak a small number of Engineers behind enemy lines."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL38
	"Once there, have them capture the Soviet structures so that you can use their own forces against them. Honor the late Emperor's dreams."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL39
	"Commander, the Soviets are reinforcing their attacks from a small outpost in the northwestern region of this area."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL40
	"Disguise your transport as one of the Soviet reinforcement vehicles and rendezvous with them.[4.9]We expect they will lead you straight to the unprotected edge of their base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL41
	"Your Sudden Transport has been destroyed.[2.3]It was key to the success of this mission.[4.7]You have failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL42
	"You've lost too many Engineers.[2.2]They were essential to the mission.[4.1]Mission aborted."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL43
	"Your base of operations has been wiped out.[2.6]The mission has failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL44
	"Commander Kenji's forces have been annihilated.[2.5]You have failed Prince Tatsu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL45
	"Your transport has arrived behind enemy lines.[2.8]Capture the Soviet production facilities."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL46
	"Now that you have access to military forces, use them to break the Soviet front lines."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL47
	"Caution -- The Soviets are using an experimental vehicle they call the Grinder to overrun our defense forces.[6.2]Prince Tatsu asks that you destroy all of these prototypes."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL48
	"The Soviet invasion force has failed and we have held our ground.[3.4]Your mission is a success."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL49
	"Commander, the Soviets have a V.I.P. bunker located in a small base to the west.[4.8]Capture that bunker to bring the base under your control."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL50
	"Now that the Soviets' base has been destroyed, finish off their remaining Grinder vehicles before they cause more harm."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL51
	"The Soviet reinforcements will continue unless their outpost to the northwest is destroyed.[5]Take down their outpost as quickly as possible."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALINTEL52
	"Commander Kenji is holding off the Soviet assault.[3]You are his reinforcements-[4.9]-prevent the Soviets from overwhelming his base, or they will push deeper into Imperial domain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALSOLDIER09
	"Those tanks are just crushing everything!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALSOLDIER10
	"What are those monstrosities?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALSOLDIER11
	"There's too many of them, retreat and regroup!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALSOLDIER12
	"Fall back! "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALSOLDIER13
	"Defend the base at all costs![1.8]We can't let them take the area!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALSOLDIER14
	"The Commander has succeeded![1.7]He's taken their forces and are using them against the Soviets!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI01_IMPERIALSOLDIER15
	"Chaaarrrgge!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL49
	"The Soviets are making a play for control of Oki Island and the Allies have turned a deaf ear to our request for help. They show no regard for the sanctity of this place."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL50
	"As the resting place of our emperors, Oki Island is the ancestral pride of our nation and must remain under our control."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL51
	"Your mission is to stop the Soviets from desecrating our Imperial tombs and from getting a foothold over these islands. You may need to use the Allies' own forces to do this. Honor the late Emperor's will."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL52
	"The Allies have a small outpost here, which you may be able to use to your advantage.[4.5]Commandeer their vehicles and stage an ambush against the incoming Soviets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL53
	"The Steel Ronin have come to fight for you to the last.[3.2]They are bound to guarding these tombs as penance and may yet regain their honor in this battle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL54
	"Now that you have acquired the Allies' field artillery vehicles,[3.2]position them along the coast at the designated points."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL55
	"Once there, use their special ability to deploy them, so that they may bombard the Soviets from long range."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL56
	"The Soviets are responding to our attacks by moving in on the Emperor's Tomb.[4]It must not fall.[5.5]Defend it at all cost, and eliminate the remaining Soviet forces here."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL57
	"The Emperor's Tomb is taking heavy fire.[2.2]Do not let it fall."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL58
	"Soviet forces inbound.[1.2]Begin the assault as soon as you make visual contact."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL59
	"An Imperial Tomb is under heavy fire.[2.3]Stop the Soviets from desecrating our land."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL60
	"An Imperial Tomb has fallen."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL61
	"You have lost too many forces in order to complete your objectives.[3.4]Mission aborted."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL62
	"Your forces have been defeated.[1.8]You have dishonored the Imperial lineage and failed this mission."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL63
	"You have failed to defend the Emperor's Tomb.[2.5]Aborting mission."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL64
	"An Observation Post has been destroyed.[2.4]It was a critical structure in the claiming of this region.[5.1]Mission aborted."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL65
	"The Soviets are making a play for control of Oki Island and the Allies have turned a deaf ear to our request for help. They show no regard for the sancity of this place."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALINTEL66
	"As the resting place of our emperors, Oki Island is the ancestral pride of our nation and must remain under our control."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALSOLDIER09
	"We claim this tank in the name of the Empire!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALSOLDIER10
	"I'm sure the Allies won't miss one more IFV gone from their base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALSOLDIER11
	"Take the vehicle--it's on our soil!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALSOLDIER12
	"Time to defend the Empire once again."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALSOLDIER13
	"The Soviets are incoming, defend the Emperor's Tomb!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALSOLDIER14
	"They're getting closer to the Emperor's Tomb![1.9]Quickly, take them out!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALSOLDIER15
	"This area is clear.[1.2]Time to setup defenses."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALSOLDIER16
	"Another area locked down.[1.5]We'll have these islands back in no time."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALSOLDIER17
	"Need reinforcements up here!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI02_IMPERIALSOLDIER18
	"They're too many Soviets here, we can't hold our position!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_ALLIEDSOLDIER01
	"You're not supposed to be here![1.7]Now get back to your island and leave this to us pros!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_ALLIEDSOLDIER02
	"We've got this under control.[1.6]Pack up and go back to Japan!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_ALLIEDSOLDIER03
	"Soviets inbound! Take them out now!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_ALLIEDSOLDIER04
	"You Empire scum won't get rid of us that easily."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_ALLIEDSOLDIER05
	"We've been given the retreat order.[1.4]Pack up and move out!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL34
	"Commander, the Soviets have the entire area occupied. You'll need to get a hold of some land to allow for full base production."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL35
	"Eliminate this Soviet frontline base and use the land as a staging area for your assault."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL36
	"One of the Soviet commanders is attempting a retreat.[3]Destroy the fleeing forces before they're able to regroup and reestablish a base to the northwest."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL37
	"The Soviet base that launched the attacks on our land is vulnerable.[3.7]It must be destroyed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL38
	"Caution -- the Allies are attempting to intervene in this battle.[3.5]They are to be treated as a threat. Continue with this mission."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL39
	"Commander -- Prince Tatsu has cleared you to use the newly-designed Giga-Fortress.[4.5]It switches between sea and air forms to devastate anything in the Soviet arsenal."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL40
	"You now have authorized clearance to construct Giga-Fortress Cores from your Imperial Docks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL41
	"The Soviets' attack on the Oki Islands shall not go unpunished, on order of Prince Tatsu. You are being given the honor of retaliating against the Soviet commanders responsible."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL42
	"Your target will be the Soviet port of Vladivostok, which is the staging area for the recent Soviet attacks on our territory. Here are your objectives:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL43
	"Destroy Commander Oleg's base of operations. He's in charge of the Union's armor divisions."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL44
	"Destroy Commander Moskvin's base of operations. Many of the Union's experimental weapons are under his command."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL45
	"The Allies may not sit idly by once the fighting begins. They must not interrupt our plans."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL46
	"Do this and honor the memory of our Emperor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALINTEL47
	"Our Archer Maidens have sworn to aid you this day.[3]Their powered greatbows should be useful against the enemy's airforce."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALSOLDIER01
	"Get back here, you cowards!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALSOLDIER02
	"The Giga-Fortress is here.[1.9]Now victory will truly be ours!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALSOLDIER03
	"More Twinblades incoming, look out!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALSOLDIER04
	"This area's clear, let's keep going!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALSOLDIER05
	"Arrogant Allies, always coming in trying to take all the glory."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MI03_IMPERIALSOLDIER06
	"Can't believe we're having to fight these guys as well as the Soviets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_ARCHERMAIDEN
	"Archer Maidens use their powered greatbows to strike enemy ground and air targets.[4.7]These bows can be extremely damaging in spite of being relatively slow on the draw.[9.5]The Maidens' special ability launches an energy arrow barrage that can strike multiple targets in an area."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_BURSTDRONE
	"Burst Drones are flying robotic scouts used to survey enemy troop movements.[5]They may attach themselves to enemy vehicles, slowing the enemy down.[9.4]Burst Drones may also self-destruct, damaging nearby targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_ENGINEER
	"Engineers can instantly capture neutral or enemy structures, either on land or at sea.[5.2]They may also repair damaged structures.[7.8]Their special ability is to sprint.[10.7]After this brief burst of energy, they run out of breath and have to take a moment to recover."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_GIGAFORTRESS
	"Giga-Fortresses are among the most powerful weapons the Empire has ever developed.[4.7]In their primary form, their multiple cannons and photon rocket launchers are enough to overwhelm entire naval strike groups.[12.1]They may also switch to a secondary form, a devastating long-range artillery platform that can fly wherever it pleases."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_KINGONI
	"The King Oni are the Empire's heaviest ground forces.[3.3]These battlewalkers can incinerate foes with their eyeblasters.[7.8]Their special ability is the bull rush, which they use to close the distance with enemies,[12.5]or more often, to smash right into them and destroy them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_MCV
	"Mobile Construction Vehicles are amphibious self-powered bases that were reverse-engineered from Allied and Soviet counterparts.[7.8]They unpack into Construction Yards, which produce the nanocores that in turn convert to other Imperial structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_MECHATENGU
	"The Mecha Tengu are versatile fast-attack skirmishers whose twin autocannons are particularly deadly against infantry.[6.9]There is no terrain they cannot cross.[10]Their special ability is to transform into the Jet Tengu, a flying form effective against aircraft."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_MECHKING
	"The Shogun Executioner is a one-of-a-kind weapon.[3]This colossal battle robot was created to instill panic and awe in the enemy while taking on entire armies.[9.6]It may engage multiple forces at once with its various weapons systems, and can crush almost anything under its massive feet.[16.9]It does require anti-aircraft support, however."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_NAGINATACRUISER
	"Naginata Cruisers are specially made to destroy enemy ships in a hail of torpedoes.[5.6]Their special ability launches a spread of auxilliary torpedoes from hidden launch bays.[10.6]This attack takes considerable time to rearm."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_NANOCORE
	"Nanocores are portable structures.[2.2]They can traverse land or sea, then unfurl into a full-sized structure where needed.[7.8]Because Cores can go almost anywhere, this provides Imperial bases with great flexibility.[13.4]Note that Cores cannot pack up once unfurled."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_ORECOLLECTOR
	"Ore Collectors are amphibious resource-gathering vehicles that travel between Ore Mines and Ore Refineries.[6.4]They must be protected at all times.[9.3]They can bring up a rapid-fire weapon to defend themselves as needed, although they cannot gather ore while this security system is activated."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_ROCKETANGEL
	"Rocket Angels are flying women warriors armed with photon rocket arrays, which are effective against armored targets both on the ground and in the air.[8.8]They may switch to using an energized Paralysis Whip, which stops a single target from moving or attacking."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_SEAWING
	"Sea-Wings combine the functions of an anti-aircraft submarine with a close-air-support aircraft.[6.2]They must surface to attack in Sea-Wing form, whereas in Sky-Wing form, these units may attack relentlessly against ground or sea targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_SHINOBI
	"Shinobi are expert infiltrator-assassins.[3]Their bladed weapons are lethal to infantry and they can traverse land and sea with equal ease.[9.1]Their special ability is a smoke bomb, which causes enemies to lose the Shinobi as a target.[14.4]If a Shinobi gets inside an enemy structure, he will disrupt the enemy in various ways depending on the structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_SHOGUNBATTLESHIP
	"Shogun Battleships are the finest vessels in the Imperial fleet.[3.8]Nothing can stand up to a barrage from their six main guns.[7.9]Their special ability provides a temporary burst of speed, allowing these ships to crash straight through other vessels."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_STEELRONIN
	"The Steel Ronin are pilot-assisted robots built to withstand heavy fire in order to get within striking distance, where their polearms can slash through multiple targets in one stroke.[10.8]The Ronin's special ability sends a wave of energy coursing through the earth, damaging all in its path."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_STRIKERVX
	"Striker-VXes are dual-form pilot-assisted robots designed to destroy enemy aircraft with their guided rockets.[6.6]But that is not all.[8.3]Their special ability is to transform into the flying Chopper-VX form, which is effective against armored targets on the ground.[15.5]Nothing is safe from these units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_SUDDENTRANSPORT
	"Sudden Transports may disguise themselves as other vehicles to sneak Imperial infantry behind enemy lines.[6.7]Because they hover, they can cross land or sea equally as well.[11]Though unarmed with conventional weapons, Sudden Transports are rigged to explode if destroyed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_TANKBUSTER
	"Tankbusters are specially trained and outfitted to take on enemy armor.[3.9]Their personal plasma-cutter cannons can punch through a battle tank quickly.[8.7]Their special ability is to dive into a spider-hole, which boosts their defense and prevents them from being crushed by vehicles.[15.2]They can pop up to resume firing."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_TSUNAMITANK
	"Tsunami Tanks are amphibious, fast-firing armored units that can quickly bring ruin to enemy bases and their military vehicles.[7.7]Their special ability briefly provides a boost to their defensive strength, though they cannot fire in this state.[13.6]They can still crush infantry under their treads, however."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_WARRIOR
	"Imperial Warriors fight using burst-firing rifles specially made to take down other infantry.[6.4]Their special ability gives them a window of opportunity to rush enemy infantry with beam katanas at the ready.[12.7]One stroke from these blades is lethal."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_WAVEFORCE
	"Wave-Force Artillery are mobile bombardment vehicles that fire energy salvoes rather than basic ballistic warheads.[7.2]Their attack is extremely powerful though the firing sequence is slow.[10.9]However, their special ability lets them fire immediately--at the expense of some attack strength."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_YARIMINISUB
	"Yari Mini-Subs are undersea scouts armed with tiny torpedoes effective against enemy naval forces.[6.6]These units must surface to fire but are invulnerable to most attacks while undersea.[11.4]Their special ability causes them to self-destruct into their targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MIIN_YURIKO
	"Yuriko Omega is our most powerful infantry unit.[3.3]She has been trained to use her mind as a weapon, and her mind can destroy almost anything.[9.3]She may pursue her enemies either on land or at sea.[12.6]Should she be outnumbered, she can send her foes flying using her Psychokinetic Burst special ability."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST01
	"Thank you so much for helping me."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST02
	"I am free!  Thank you comrade."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST03
	"Oh thank goodness.[1.3]I was beginning to think I would never be rescued!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST04
	"Comrades!  Oh, it is good to be free again."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST05
	"If you come closer, I can take try to patch that wound."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST06
	"Stand next to me, and I will heal you as best I can."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST07
	"Come here and let me dress your wounds."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST08
	"While in captivity, I worked on designs for a devastating artillery shell.[5.1]Whatever these Allied dogs are building, it cannot be good."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST09
	"They forced me to develop a long range firing mechanism, but for what I don't know.[5.1]Be careful my comrades."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST10
	"This new vehicle the Allies are building has powerful anti-infantry weapons.[4.5]If by chance we should encounter it, be sure to stay far away."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST11
	"Help me!  I am under attack!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST12
	"I am in danger, Comrades!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SCIENTIST13
	"They shot me!  Help!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL58
	"Sources in the area indicate that the Allies are experimenting with new technology."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL59
	"We need to rendezvous with these sources and rally their support."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL60
	"FutureTech is the brains behind the Allies' cryo and chrono weaponry, amongst others."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL61
	"Some of our experimental Desolator Troopers were sent in but all contact has been cut off.[5.8]Be on the lookout for survivors."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL62
	"Several Soviet scientists have been kidnapped and put to work by the Allies on their experiments.[5.3]Find and rescue them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL63
	"Caution:Unidentified energy signatures readings detected.[3.7]Please stand by."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL64
	"It appears the Allies have activated the Pacifiers, their new long-range artillery vehicles.[5.6]Any forces in range are strongly advised to avoid standing still."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL65
	"Commander -- the safe return of the Soviet chief scientists is your primary objective."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL66
	"The mission is in danger.[1.5]The chief scientists must be delivered to the harbor safely."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL67
	"Our forces are waiting at the harbor.[2.1]Get the chief scientists to safety as quickly as possible."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL68
	"You found one of our Desolator Troopers, who is now yours to command.[4.2]Desolators specialize in urban warfare and close combat against unarmored targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL69
	"Desolators can spray poison on enemy infantry and clear garrisoned buildings as well."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL70
	"The Desolator Trooper's special ability lets him attack vehicles and other targets with an explosive and unstable poison ordnance."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL71
	"Please stand by for reinforcements."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL72
	"Reinforcements are en route, Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL73
	"The Chief Scientists have perished.[2.2]Their knowledge was essential to our plans.[4.5]Mission failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL74
	"Your combat reconnaissance forces have been killed in action.[3.3]Aborting mission."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL75
	"We need you to investigate Allied activity in Romania and find a way to rescue our Chief Scientists. You will lead this recovery force. Their objectives are as follows:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL76
	"Capture the Observation Posts to assess the Allies' intentions."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL77
	"Recover our Chief Scientists being held in this area against their will."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL78
	"Return the Chief Scientists safely to the harbor for extraction."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL79
	"Good hunting."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL80
	"Conscripts can use their Molotov Cocktails to kill enemies inside of garrisoned buildings."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL81
	"Flak Troopers can use their Magnetic Mines to inflict heavy damage on enemy vehicles."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL82
	"Moving units inside the radius of the Athena Cannon's shield is a good way to bypass it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL83
	"Tesla Troopers can use their EM Disruptors ability to disable any vehicles near to them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL84
	"The Desolator Trooper can spray poison at enemies garrisoned inside buildings to clear them out."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL85
	"The Desolator Trooper can switch to using his Splattershot Gun to deal with enemy vehicles.[5.1]Just one shot causes vehicles to rapidly take damage."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL86
	"Sources in the area indicate that an Allied weapons supplier, FutureTech Corporation, is experimenting with new technology here."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL87
	"Several of our Chief Scientists are being forced to work against their will on new weapons technology in this area.[6.5]Find and rescue them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS01_SOVIETINTEL88
	"FutureTech have activated the Pacifiers, their new long-range artillery vehicles.[4.8]Any forces in range are strongly advised to avoid standing still."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL21
	"Those are Soviet civilians FutureTech is using in their experiments.[3.9]We need to end this."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL22
	"Stand down, Commander.[1.6]Kirov Airships are on their way in to level the area."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL23
	"Caution -- Kirov air fleet under attack by unknown forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL24
	"Commander -- FutureTech knows we're here and are sending assault forces.[4.4]Your only chance is to order your units to retreat back to the village and stand your ground there."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL25
	"Dispatching reinforcements as soon as possible -- you must hold and defend your position until the reinforcements arrive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL26
	"FutureTech has set up a facility on the river to the north. Infiltrate the area and find out what they're up to."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL27
	"Reinforcements have arrived.[2]Use them to recover the old base, then level the FutureTech facilities here."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL28
	"The gulags imprisoning Soviet citizens are also holding tanks.[4.1]Recover them to add to your forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL29
	"The FutureTech structures hold valuable intelligence.[3.4]Recover it by capturing each structure with a Combat Engineer."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL30
	"All the FutureTech facilities in the area have been destroyed.[3.7]Well done, Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL31
	"All prisoners have been liberated.[2.1]The Soviet people are grateful, Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL32
	"We've recovered all of the FutureTech intel.[2.6]You are cleared to destroy the facility immediately."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL33
	"Mortar Cycles from a nearby military base have arrived to aid you with their explosive firepower. Plans to construct additional Cycles have been sent to your War Factory."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL34
	"Our infiltration team has been lost. Aborting mission."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL35
	"The abandoned base has been destroyed.[2.3]There's no way we can mount a counter-attack now.[5.3]Mission failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL36
	"The FutureTech forces proved overwhelming.[2.7]We have failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL37
	"Beware when engaging FutureTech's elite infantry, the Cryo Legionnaires.[4.6]They defeated our Kirovs and are surely as dangerous against ground forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL38
	"Incoming Cryo Legionnaires.[1.8]Their lack of speed appears to be their only weakness."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL39
	"Our agents have discovered that FutureTech Corporation has a research facility on our own soil, in Murmansk."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL40
	"You are needed to lead a reconnaissance force in that area to determine the enemy threat. Your objective is simple:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL41
	"Infiltrate the FutureTech research facility. We need more information about their plans."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL42
	"Stand by for further orders in the field. Proceed with care -- we have limited information about FutureTech's defenses in this region."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL43
	"You will need your War Bears to reach the vantage point indicated.[3.5]Keep them alive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL44
	"We've lost the War Bears needed to scout out the FutureTech base.[3.7]Aborting mission."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETINTEL45
	"Reinforcements are inbound.[1.8]Use them to fortify your defenses, then assault the FutureTech facilities."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETSOLDIER04
	"Watch out for the patrols!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETSOLDIER05
	"More patrols!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETSOLDIER06
	"We can get a good view from the ledge up this hill."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETSOLDIER07
	"So cold. Why must we always fight in the snow?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETSOLDIER08
	"Stop complaining. At least bears have fur coats."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS02_SOVIETSOLDIER09
	"We can garrison the buildings in the area for added protection."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL19
	"We must use caution when assaulting this FutureTech stronghold.[3.6]The might of the Soviet military is cut off from this area so your forces are limited."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL20
	"The first step is to eliminate any opposing forces on each island, including their Lookout Posts.[6]We must gain a foothold here before we can launch a proper attack."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL21
	"The first island has been cleared.[2.2]We are sending through a small reinforcement force now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL22
	"The second island is now clear.[2.1]A small reinforcement team is being dispatched to the area."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL23
	"The third and final island is ours.[2.6]Commander, a Construction Vehicle is en route to your location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL24
	"We need to acquire some resources in order to secure our position.[3.9]We have a plan for this:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL25
	"We have learned that FutureTech is expecting a large shipment of ore to fund the production of its military forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL26
	"Your objective is to intercept these shipments before they reach their destination.[4.4]Eliminate the inbound Prospectors to collect their cargo."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL27
	"Once the resources are yours, waste no time in preparing an attack force with which to destroy FutureTech's facilities here.[7.5]Expect fierce resistance."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL28
	"Too many of FutureTech's resource shipments have broken through. Mission failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL29
	"Destroy the in-bound Prospectors.[2.3]Each one that reaches its destination allows FutureTech to construct more weapons to use against us."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL30
	"It appears that FutureTech has been alerted to your presence.[3.3]This concludes the infiltration phase of this mission.[6.5]Begin the assault, and good luck."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL31
	"Caution -- FutureTech is using a Chronosphere to transport ground vehicles across the water."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL32
	"Commander -- sources indicate several large, unidentified aircraft are entering the battlefield.[5.5]These are not our forces, prepare to defend yourself."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL33
	"Your primary objective is to destroy the FutureTech facilities here."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL34
	"We managed to secure a heavy prototype of the Sickle, which may be useful to you.[4.7]It had an effective design but proved too costly to mass-produce."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL35
	"The Reaper should be effective against FutureTech's vehicles.[3.4]Use caution when using the Reaper's leaping special ability --[7.1]it was never fully field-tested."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL36
	"Your strike team has been eliminated.[2.3]We have lost our opportunity to strike at FutureTech.[5.8]Mission failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL37
	"Your forces have been destroyed.[2]This was our only chance to stop this threat."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL38
	"We have discovered a FutureTech military base in the Yucatan. It is the origin of forces that attacked in Siberia, and thus it is a threat and must be eliminated."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL39
	"A strike team under your command will lead the assault. Your mission objectives are:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL40
	"Bring down the Lookout Posts around the island. This will allow us to provide additional reinforcements without giving away our position."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL41
	"Intercept FutureTech's supply lines. We will use their own resources against them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL42
	"Eliminate the FutureTech military base and any of its new weapons."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL43
	"Tread lightly, Commander. The element of surprise is likely to be our only advantage during this operation."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL44
	"The Allies have carelessly placed explosive barrels next to vital structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL45
	"If you select a Terror Drone inside an enemy vehicle and give it a move order, it will move there as soon as it's done destroying that vehicle.[8]Use this tactic to keep your Drones safe."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS03_SOVIETINTEL46
	"Switch a Terror Drone to its stasis weapon to lock enemy vehicles in place and prevent them from retreating."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL35
	"This is it, Commander.[1.4]We've tracked FutureTech to this island, where they are developing their new weapons in the shadow of the Sigma Harmonizer."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL36
	"Additional FutureTanks incoming.[2.2]You need to destroy all of the factories."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL37
	"A Cooling Tower has been captured.[1.9]That will slow their production."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL38
	"Holding this Cooling Tower should slow their FutureTank production speed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL39
	"Keep control of the Cooling Tower and we'll hinder their produciton of FutureTanks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL40
	"FutureTech has re-captured a Cooling Tower.[2.8]Their production speed will increase."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL41
	"A factory has been captured.[1.9]Intel is being sent to our chief scientists.[4.2]Keep at it, Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL42
	"Another factory has been captured.[2.1]This intelligence will be useful to the reconstruction of the Union."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL43
	"That should be all of FutureTech's intelligence.[2.6]Well done, Commander.[3.7]Please proceed to eliminate that factory."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL44
	"We cannot land on the island yet.[2]You will have to establish a base on the mainland to the east."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL45
	"Now that our Construction Yard is set up, focus on taking out the factories building FutureTech's weapons."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL46
	"The Cooling Towers scattered around the island keep the factories at maximum efficiency.[5]Capture them to slow production of the FutureTanks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL47
	"Allied aircraft dominate the coast.[2.3]We cannot spare any aircraft until the airbase has been destroyed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL48
	"Information in the factories could be used to help bring the Soviet Union to its former glory.[5.5]Gather their intel by capturing them before you raze them to the ground."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL49
	"Commander -- you have just received emergency clearance to use Grinders, one of our experimental forces.[6]They may improve your chances against the FutureTanks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL50
	"All FutureTech facilities offline and their remaining forces are in a state of disarray.[5.2]Commander -- the day is won."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL51
	"We've lost our Construction Vehicle.[2]We cannot continue against FutureTech.[4.2]Aborting mission."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL52
	"Grinders are amphibious armored vehicle with no conventional weapons, but they can tear apart anything they get close to."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL53
	"Our main target is a massive structure called the Sigma Harmonizer. It is the culmination of FutureTech's research, with capabilities our intel can only guess. We now know where it is, and are preparing a full-scale assault."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL54
	"Here is what we need you to do:"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL55
	"Bring down the coastal defenses protecting the Sigma Harmonizer. This will give our main assault forces the signal to move in."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL56
	"Destroy FutureTech's research and production facilities. Leave nothing standing."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL57
	"Then focus on destroying the Sigma Harmonizer before it has completed its startup sequence. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL58
	"Completing this mission should cause FutureTech to suffer irreparable setbacks, and expose their self-serving plot to all the world. Good hunting."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL59
	"All our forces in this region have been lost.[2.8]The mission is failed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL60
	"We've tracked Future Tech to the nearby island, where they are developing their new weapons in the shadow of the Sigma Harmonizer."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL61
	"We cannot land on the island yet. You will have to establish a base on the mainland to the west."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL62
	"Grinders are heavily armored vehicles with no conventional weapons, but they can tear apart anything they get close to."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL63
	"Massive power surge detected.[2]This must be the Sigma Harmonizer powering up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL64
	"Warning -- our clocks now seem to be out of sync with the world. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL65
	"Caution -- The Sigma Harmonizer has been activated.[3.2]None of our forces are responding![5.2]Battlefield control terminating."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL66
	"Re-establishing battlefield control.[2.4]FutureTech is unable to sustain the effects of the Sigma Harmonizer for long.[6.8]However, they are preparing to use it again."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL67
	"Warning -- Energy readings from the Sigma Harmonizer are stabilizing.[4.2]FutureTech will be able to use it more and more often.[7.2]You must hurry to prevent this."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL68
	"Caution -- FutureTech has re-activated the Sigma Harmonizer."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MS04_SOVIETINTEL69
	"Caution -- Sigma Harmonizer activated.[2.6]Battlefield control temporarily shutting down."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_AKULASUB
	"Akula Subs excel at quickly destroying enemy ships with their torpedoes.[5]They must surface to fire, but are invulnerable to most attacks while submerged.[10.3]Their special ability is to launch ultratorpedoes, which are devastating unguided warheads that rapidly accelerate straight ahead."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_APOCALYPSETANK
	"Apocalypse Tanks can easily take on other vehicles with their powerful main guns, and can crush most anything under their massive treads.[9.4]Their special ability is a magnetic harpoon, which can draw enemy vehicles in for the kill."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_BULLFROG
	"Bullfrogs are amphibious anti-aircraft troop transports.[4.1]Their flak cannons can quickly destroy enemy aircraft.[8.4]The only means for passengers to exit a Bullfrog is via the \"man cannon\", which can be used to launch infantry behind enemy lines."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_CONSCRIPT
	"Conscripts are the Union's mainline anti-infantry forces.[4.4]They are not well-trained but can be effective in numbers.[8.4]They carry assault rifles and can also switch to using Molotov cocktails, which are more effective against structures, including garrisons."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_DESOLATOR
	"Desolator Troopers are heavy infantry who fight using corrosive poisons stored in their chemical suits.[5.3]Contact with these poisons is almost instantly fatal to unprotected targets.[9.2]Desolator Troopers can either spray their toxins or launch them in explosive globs."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_DESOLATOR1
	"Desolator Troopers are heavy infantry who fight using deadly poisons stored in their chemical suits.[6]They can either spray their toxins on infantry or switch to their splattershot mode to launch explosive globs of corrosive acids against vehicles.[14.4]Their spray can also clear out enemy garrisons."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_DREADNOUGHT
	"Dreadnoughts are powerful long-range bombardment ships armed with multiple rocket launchers.[6]They can destroy any surface target in moments.[9.7]Their special ability makes them fire even more rapidly, although forcing the weapons systems to do this gradually causes internal damage."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_ENGINEER
	"Combat Engineers can capture neutral or enemy structures both on land or at sea, or repair your damaged structures.[7.7]They carry basic revolvers for self-defense.[11.3]Their special ability is to build a Battle Bunker, which can be garrisoned by other infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_FLAKTROOPER
	"Flak Troopers are convicts forced to carry out their sentence by fighting with heavy weapons on the front lines.[6.7]They are most effective against aircraft.[9.8]They can switch to using magnetic mines that work well against vehicles.[14.7]These mines will also detonate should a vehicle crush the Flak Trooper."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_GRINDER
	"Grinders are heavily-armored amphibious vehicles that lack conventional weapons but can simply roll over most smaller targets.[8]They can tear apart larger targets almost as quickly.[11.4]Their special ability gives them a temporary burst of speed, allowing them to overrun faster foes and deal more damage."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_GRINDER1
	"Grinders are heavily-armored amphibious vehicles that lack conventional weapons but can simply roll over most smaller targets.[7.5]They can tear apart larger targets almost as quickly.[10.9]Their special ability gives them a temporary burst of speed, allowing them to overrun faster foes."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_HAMMERTANK
	"Hammer Tanks are effective against most vehicles and structures.[4.4]Further, they can crush infantry under their treads.[8.4]Instead of using their main gun, they can switch to using the Leech Beam, which absorbs enemy armor.[14.6]The beam can steal enemy weapons as well."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_KIROV
	"Kirov Airships are flying heavy bombers.[3.1]Nothing on the ground can withstand their bombs.[6.1]Kirovs are slow but highly durable.[9.3]Their special ability provides them with a burst of speed using a chemical process that slowly causes them to take damage.[18.2]Therefore it must be used sparingly."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_MCV
	"Mobile Construction Vehicles are amphibious mobile bases.[4.2]They are critical to battlefield operations, even though they have no weapons of their own.[9.6]Once unpacked into Construction Yards, they can build all facilities authorized by the Soviet war council.[16.6]They must be defended by any means necessary."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_MIGFIGHTER
	"MiG Fighters are specialized air-superiority jets, designed purely for intercepting groups of enemy aircraft.[7.9]They carry a limited supply of ammunition and must occasionally rearm at an Airbase.[13.6]They have a special ability to rapidly return to base if needed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_MORTARCYCLE
	"Mortar Cycles are light artillery vehicles that excel at hit-and-run attacks versus enemy fortifications or slower forces.[7.8]They may quickly switch between using Molotov cocktails to burn their foes to a crisp, or raining down explosive shells with their mortar attack."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_NATASHA
	"Natasha is the Union's greatest sniper-commando, whose rifle can kill several infantry in one shot.[7.2]She may also call in airstrikes against other targets.[11.5]Her special ability is to snipe pilots cleanly in their vehicles, such that the vehicles can then be captured.[18.8]Natasha is equally effective on land or at sea."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_ORECOLLECTOR
	"Ore Collectors automatically gather resources essential to fueling the Soviet War Machine.[5.9]These amphibious vehicles must be protected at all costs.[9.9]Their special ability is to deploy reactive armor, which makes them highly resistant to enemy attacks.[17]Note they cannot gather resources in this state."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_REAPER
	"Reapers are bigger, tougher predecessors of the Sickle.[3.4]They are equipped with multiple grenade and rocket launchers, effective against multiple armored targets.[9.1]Their special ability is to jump, but their legs tend to break on impact.[13.7]As such, Reapers still serve well as fixed gun emplacements."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_REAPER1
	"Reapers are bigger, tougher predecessors of the Sickle.[3.5]They are equipped with multiple grenade and rocket launchers, and are effective against multiple smaller targets, including aircraft.[10.7]Their special ability is to jump, but their legs tend to break on impact.[15.3]As such, Reapers still serve well as fixed gun emplacements."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_SCIENTIST
	"Soviet Chief Scientists have been plucked from the ranks of the Union's finest scientific minds and forced to work for the FutureTech Corporation against their will.[9.4]They are unfit for combat and must be protected.[12.6]However, they do have medical supplies, so they can heal friendly infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_SICKLE
	"Sickles are fast-moving anti-personnel vehicles armed with three independently-firing machine guns.[7.3]Their special ability lets them leap long distances, or even onto enemy infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_SPUTNIK
	"Sputniks are defenseless vehicles that offer an economical alternative to Mobile Construction Vehicles when it becomes necessary to expand.[9.6]These amphibious units may convert to an Outpost almost anywhere, allowing other Soviet structures to be built nearby."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_STINGRAY
	"Stingrays are experimental strike craft fitted with Tesla weapons that are effective against most targets.[6.7]Stingrays are amphibious, though slower-moving on land.[10.8]Their special ability is the Tesla Surge, which shoots lightning in all directions while briefly immobilizing the unit.[18]It only works on water."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_TERRORDRONE
	"Terror Drones are amphibious robots that can kill enemy infantry or tear into vehicles and dismantle them from the inside.[8.2]Once infected, the vehicle must be repaired, or else it will be destroyed.[13.2]Terror Drones can switch to using an electro-stasis ray that shuts down vehicle locomotors, preventing them from moving."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_TESLATANK
	"Tesla Tanks are experimental vehicles whose dual Tesla coil weapons are more powerful than most any conventional weapon.[8.7]Like Tesla Troopers, Tesla Tanks may switch to using electromagnetic disrupters that disable enemy vehicles nearby."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_TESLATROOPER
	"Tesla Troopers are heavy infantry armed with electrifying weapons effective against most targets.[6.7]They are too big to be crushed by most tanks.[10.2]Their special ability is to switch to using electromagnetic disrupters that automatically disable enemy vehicles in the vicinity."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_TWINBLADE
	"Twinblades are anti-surface combat helicopters armed with machine guns and rockets.[6.6]In addition to their powerful weapons, Twinblades function as transports, and can ferry infantry or some vehicles across the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_V4ROCKETLNCHR
	"V4 Rocket Launchers are long-range artillery pieces whose rockets can quickly destroy most any unit or structure, if they hit.[9.5]Their special ability is to fire multiwarheads that split up in flight, causing widespread damage.[16.3]Note V4s cannot defend themselves up close."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MSIN_WARBEAR
	"War Bears are trained for scouting by land and sea, as well as anti-infantry combat.[5.6]Their mauling attack is lethal against most infantry.[9.3]Their special ability is an amplified roar that causes paralysis in enemy infantry within earshot.[16.5]War Bears also detect disguised enemy units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN01
	"*Oy, welcome to Command & Conquer Red Alert 3."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN02
	"*I'm an Allied Guardian Tank, and these prats and I are here to tell you about how we think you should be doing your job. Sir."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN03
	"*Coh, blimey…right, OK... To move your camera around the battlefield, just hold down the right mouse button and slide your mouse around."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN05
	"*Easy enough."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN06
	"*Now, to rotate the camera, hold down the middle mouse button and move the mouse around."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN08
	"*To zoom the camera in and out, simply slide your mouse wheel."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN09
	"*To zoom the camera in and out, simply move the right stick up or down."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN10
	"*As you go about fussing with the camera, sir, remember you can always click the middle mouse button to reset the viewing angle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN12
	"*Right proper, you have. Objectives, as you might have surmised, are special goals you need to accomplish in order to progress through the campaigns."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN13
	"*If at any time you're not sure what in blazes you're supposed to be doing, hit the Escape key to pay a visit to the mission menu. It'll list all your current objectives."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN15
	"*Right. To select a unit, just left-click on it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN17
	"*Nice. He's definitely one of ours, sir."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN18
	"*I was getting to that."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN19
	"*To move your units, whilst having them selected, click the right mouse button on any open terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN21
	"*Erm... Right, so, to issue an Attack Order to your units, whilst having them selected, put your cursor over a target and click the right mouse button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN23
	"*Bloody robots."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN24
	"*Now, in addition to issuing attack commands on specific targets, you can have your units move and attack any enemies along the way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_GUARDIAN25
	"*Now that's a fine job you did there, Commander! You now know how to move around the battlefield as well as how to make your forces shoot their enemies dead."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER01
	"*Yes. We have temporarily called a truce to make sure you do not send us to our deaths needlessly."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER02
	"*To begin with, we will tell you how to move your viewpoint around the battlefield and how to command your units, including the best ones such as me, the Soviet Hammer Tank!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER03
	"*Just look this body compared with the teeny little Japanese tank to my left."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER04
	"*Ow!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER05
	"*You may also move your cursor to the far edges of the screen!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER06
	"*My goodness, commander! You have completed your first objective!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER07
	"*Good! Now that you have an idea for how to move around the battlefield, let's move on to controlling your units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER08
	"*Here come some of our hated enemies now!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER09
	"*You may also hold down the left mouse button and drag your mouse. This will create a selection box. Any units inside the selection box will be selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER12
	"*And if you want more units added to your selection, hold down the Shift key and drag a selection box around those units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER14
	"*OK, now that we've reminded you how to select units, you’ll need to move them around the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER15
	"*Ow!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER16
	"*See? They obey you without question!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER17
	"*They seem so real..."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER18
	"*Observe that you can distinguish your forces from the robots based on the colored blips in the Radar in the upper-right corner of your battlefield control display."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER19
	"*The color of the blips refers to the color of the different sides involved in a battle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER20
	"*Notice that as you move your mouse cursor over those dummies, it changes to an attack cursor!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER21
	"*So long you stupid robots!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER22
	"*To issue an Attack-Move command, while having your units selected, just press the A key and right-click on any open terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER23
	"*You can issue Attack-Move orders on the Radar as well!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_HAMMER28
	"*See you there!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI01
	"*Shut up!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI02
	"*Please excuse him, sir. Let us begin."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI03
	"*Try moving your camera now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI04
	"*Try rotating your camera now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI05
	"*Try zooming your camera now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI06
	"*In general, objectives will be labeled using special markers out on the battlefield. Follow the onscreen indicators to get to them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI07
	"*Try selecting one of these Allied Peacekeepers."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI08
	"*Try moving your units to the designated area up ahead."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI09
	"*Notice, Commander, how the darkened area of the battlefield revealed itself as your forces drew near."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI10
	"*This darkened area is the Fog of War, and represents parts of the battlefield that may be hiding enemy troop movements."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI11
	"*Be careful when venturing into unseen areas, and use your scouts to survey the terrain before committing your forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI12
	"*Now, up ahead are some dummy targets that you're going to destroy."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI13
	"*They resemble real-life Soviet Conscripts, but I assure you they are merely robots we created for this exercise."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI14
	"*See how foolishly they behave?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI15
	"*If you encounter different-colored blips as you clear the Fog of War, those are likely enemy forces. So be prepared."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI16
	"*If you need to take a closer look at your Radar, you can always use Radar Mode."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI19
	"*Hai, that is it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI22
	"*Destroy all the target dummies in the area."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI23
	"*Now, look there."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI24
	"*We need you to lead us to that strategic point, yet many robots stand in the way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI25
	"*If you please, issue an Attack-Move order to the strategic point. You have the command. Lead us to victory!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT01_TSUNAMI26
	"*Indeed. We suggest you move on to the next lesson on building a military base for further instruction on properly commanding an army."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN01
	"*Good to have you, Commander. In this mission, we'll be reminding you all about constructing a base for each of the factions."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN02
	"*We'll start with the Allies for obvious reasons. First things first, though."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN03
	"*On the right side of the screen is the Sidebar, which is where you manage all your base construction and unit production."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN06
	"*The Command Menu lets you do everything from build units and structures to use your units' special abilities, and much more."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN08
	"*In general, you can drill deeper or confirm selections in the Command Menu with button A, or go back up or cancel selections with button B."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN09
	"*Go ahead and get comfortable using this thing. It lets you manage all your forces and production no matter where you're focusing your attention in battle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN10
	"*Best remember to use the F hotkey as a shortcut to your units' special abilities."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN12
	"*Bear in mind that there may be impassable areas of the map where you're not allowed to place down your structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN13
	"*When you try to place a structure down over impassable or un-buildable terrain, red cells will appear on the build grid indicating that you're unable to place a structure there."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN14
	"*That's the way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN15
	"*As the name suggests, a Power Plant provides your base with power. All your structures, with the exception of your Power Plant and Construction Yard, use power."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN16
	"*You can tell how much power you've got to spare by glancing at the power meter next to your Radar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN17
	"*It's important to understand the consequences of a low-power situation."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN18
	"*While in Low Power, your units and structures will build at a reduced speed, and your base defenses won't work, so it's always good to have plenty of power as you build up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN19
	"*When you place your Ore Refinery, you get a Prospector as part of the deal, and he'll go about collecting ore for you automatically."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN20
	"*Pro tip, friend: If by some freak accident, one of your Prospectors or Ore Collectors is destroyed, you can always build another from your Ore Refineries."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN21
	"*Just select the Ore Refinery and you'll see it can build another resource vehicle as its special ability."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN22
	"*As long as your Ore Refinery is close to a mine, you only need one vehicle gathering from it, so don't waste credits making more of those little tykes than you need."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN23
	"*You now have power and an economy set up. You’re ready to start training units for the fight. From your Production Tab, go ahead and build a Boot Camp."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN24
	"*You now have power and an economy set up. You’re ready to start training units for the fight. Go ahead and open up the Command Menu and build a Boot Camp."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN25
	"*Remember to place it down by selecting its icon, then left-clicking on open terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN27
	"*Incidentally, you can rotate the face of a structure you're about to plop down by holding down the left mouse button and moving the mouse around. Let go of the button when ready."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN29
	"*Try holding the Shift key to queue up five of those blokes at a time."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN30
	"*You can set a different rally point for them by selecting the structure and right-clicking some other place."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN31
	"*All three factions produce units in the same way, from the respective tabs in the sidebar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN33
	"*All three factions produce units in the same way, from the respective queues in the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN34
	"*By the by, many of your structures aren’t restricted to being built on land. You can set 'em up on water as well."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN35
	"*If you build another Power Plant, try placing it out in the drink. It doesn't cost you any extra and most ground units won't be able to get to it that way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN36
	"*Yeah, that's it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN37
	"*Also, bear in mind that the Allies' Technology Level is local to their Construction Yards or Command Hubs."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN38
	"*That means not all your production structures on the battlefield may offer you the same construction options."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN39
	"*You can upgrade your Construction Yard or your Command Hub by clicking the Heightened Clearance button with one of these structures selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN40
	"*You can upgrade your Construction Yard or your Command Hub by selecting them, opening the Command Menu, and selecting the Heightened Clearance button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN41
	"*Try requesting Heightened Clearance on both your ConYard and your Command Hub now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN42
	"*That's it. Now the other."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN43
	"*There it is."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN44
	"*Heightened Clearance costs you, and there's even a higher clearance level after that."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN45
	"*You need to decide when and where to request better tech when commanding the Allies, else things may turn rotten."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN46
	"*Notice how the structure is hastily being thrown together in the field."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN47
	"*While it's building up, it's vulnerable to enemy attack, so be cautious when placing your structures. All Soviet structures build up in this way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN48
	"*Oy, aren't you forgetting something?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN49
	"*Haha, keep fussing with the Imperial build system if you want, and when you're all set, select me and we'll wrap up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN50
	"*Well, that concludes the lesson on base-building. Don't worry, the other ones will be shorter. Mostly. Let's shove off, lads."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_GUARDIAN51
	"*Commander, see you then."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER01
	"*Here we have one of the hated Allied Mobile Construction Vehicles. The MCV will unpack into a Construction Yard."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER02
	"*To unpack it, select it, then click on its special ability button at the bottom right of your screen. Go on, don't be shy!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER04
	"*Very fancy, no?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER05
	"*In general, special abilities are executed with the left mouse button, or canceled with the right mouse button. However, the right mouse button is used for basic orders."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER06
	"*In general, special abilities are executed with the A button, or canceled with the B button. The B button is also used to deselect units or structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER07
	"*Now that your MCV has unpacked into a Construction Yard, you should have some new construction options available to you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER08
	"*To access your production structures build queue, select the ConYard or click on the Production Tab that's flashing."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER09
	"*To access your production structures build queue, select the ConYard and open the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER10
	"*Alternatively, if you don't have anything selected, open the Command Menu and drill down to your Production Structures in the 12 o'clock position."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER11
	"*Whoa, look at what we have here! Looks like you have access to build a Power Plant!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER12
	"*Ow!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER13
	"*The next thing you'll need to get base humming along is an Ore Refinery."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER14
	"*This structure comes with a free Prospector vehicle, which will collect ore from that nearby Ore Mine."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER15
	"*To build your Ore Refinery, select the Production Tab and select the Ore Refinery button, just as you did with the Power Plant."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER16
	"*To build your Ore Refinery, open the Command Menu, navigate to your Production Structures, and press the Ore Refinery Button, just as you did with the Power Plant."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER17
	"*Now that construction is complete, click the Ore Refinery button and consider where to place it on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER18
	"*Now that construction is complete, open the Command Menu and select the Ore Refinery and consider where to place it on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER19
	"*While you're able to place your Refinery anywhere on open terrain, the optimal location is just in front of an Ore Mine."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER20
	"*You'll see those spots ghosted on the terrain. As you move your cursor over those spots, your structure preview should snap to the optimal position."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER21
	"*Then, just click to place your Ore Refinery and you're set!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER23
	"*I always wonder, though... how come the mightiest nations in the world need to collect ore while killing each other? I mean, what is even in that stuff?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER24
	"*Ow!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER25
	"*Now that you have a Boot Camp, you’re able to train some infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER26
	"*To do this, you may select either your Boot Camp or the Infantry Tab under your Radar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER27
	"*To do this, you may select either your Boot Camp and open the Command Menu, or navigate to your Infantry Queues in the 2 o'clock position in the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER28
	"*This will bring up the available units you’re able to train. Let’s train some of the so-called \"Peacekeepers.\""
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER29
	"*Select the Peacekeeper button to start training one."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER30
	"*You may queue up multiple Peacekeepers by continuing to select on his portrait."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER31
	"*Yes. Also, should you ever have need to run away like a little girl, you may pack up your ConYard, then unpack it on the water."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER32
	"*The Boot Camp and Armor Facility are the only Allied structures you may not place on the water."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER33
	"*Your Seaport, on the other hand, is the only structure you may not build on land."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER34
	"*Ow! What was that for?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER35
	"*Just like the Allies, however, you can pause and cancel a structure's build-up by right-clicking on its button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER36
	"*Just like the Allies, however, you can pause and cancel a structure's build-up by navigating to that structure in the Command Menu and using the B button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER37
	"*And of course, your Soviet structures may be placed at sea -- with the exceptions of the Barracks and War Factory."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER38
	"*Nyet! At least... not anymore."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER39
	"*Commander, one truly unique Soviet structure you should be aware of is the Crusher Crane. Try building one now from your Production Structures queue."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER40
	"*Crusher Cranes work much like Construction Yards, so now, you can build two structures at once from your two separate build queues."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER41
	"*What's more, your Crane's repair drones will automatically repair nearby vehicles, or you can order those vehicles into its grinders to crush them for a quick refund."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER42
	"*To access your newly-added build queues, click the buttons added to the Sidebar, or click the tabs in the Sidebar to cycle between queues."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER43
	"*To access your newly-added build queues, open the Command Menu with the Crusher Crane selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER44
	"*When you have multiple queues of a type available, you can cycle through them in the Command Menu by pressing the A button without moving the stick."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER45
	"*You can build multiple production structures to gain more build queues, allowing you to build more stuff at once. Of course, you'll need plenty of income to support this."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER46
	"*Now, please feel free to continue exploring the richness of the Soviet build system."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER47
	"*When you're done, please select the Tsunami Tank to proceed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER48
	"*...I still think ours is better... Oh no."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER49
	"*Ow! OW!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_HAMMER50
	"*Ow!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI01
	"*Notice that the MCV's Unpack is a targeted special ability. Targeted abilities require you to select a target by placing your cursor over the terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI02
	"*Observe the ghosted image of the Construction Yard attached to your cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI03
	"*Now left-click anywhere on open terrain to open your MCV to unpack at that location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI05
	"*Don't overdo it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI06
	"*Commander: Select the Power Plant button to begin building it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI07
	"*All Allied structures build over time inside the Construction Yard. Once they're ready, you'll be able to place them on the battlefield right away."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI08
	"*Your Power Plant is now ready to be placed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI09
	"*Simply left-click on its button and move your mouse over open terrain. Then left-click on an open spot on the terrain."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI11
	"*Bear in mind that a single Ore Refinery likely will not be enough to fund your military escapades."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI12
	"*Try to build an Ore Refinery next to each Ore Mine near your base, but be careful to defend them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI13
	"*Hai! Properly executed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI14
	"*Don't ask ridiculous questions!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI15
	"*Ore is the primary resource in Red Alert 3. Refineries automatically convert it to credits, which is the currency used to purchase all units and structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI16
	"*Ore Mines have a finite amount of resources that will eventually slow to trickle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI17
	"*So if you deplete an Ore Mine, it’s best to try and expand to another in order to maintain a steady income."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI18
	"*You can also halt the production of units or structures by right-clicking on a production button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI19
	"*Right-clicking a second time will cancel production and refund any credits that were spent. Left-clicking on a paused production process will resume production."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI20
	"*You can also halt the production of units or structures by pressing the B button while you have them highlighted in the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI21
	"*Pressing B a second time will cancel production and refund any credits that were spent. Pressing button A on a paused production process will resume production."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI22
	"*Observe, however, that Allied structures may only be built in the radius surrounding the Construction Yard."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI23
	"*You may expand your build radius by creating Command Hubs, which convert from your Prospectors."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI24
	"*Please select your Prospector and use its special ability to unpack it somewhere. Across the water, perhaps? Go ahead, commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI25
	"*Silence! Surely the Commander wants to move on to the other factions by now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI26
	"*Feel free to continue dabbling with the Allies, then select me when you are ready to continue."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI27
	"*This monstrosity is the Soviet Construction Yard. You will see that the Soviets build differently from the Allies."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI28
	"*Select the Construction Yard or the Production Tab, then select the Reactor button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI29
	"*Select the Construction Yard and open the Command Menu, or just navigate to the Production Structures queue in the Command Menu. Then select the Reactor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI30
	"*Notice how the Command Menu closed automatically, to let you make your next move."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI31
	"*Now place the Reactor on open terrain, as you did with the Allied structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI32
	"*Do not wait for the Reactor to build in the queue, for you would wait... forever!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI33
	"*Unlike the Allies, the Soviets carelessly build their structures out on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI34
	"*At last. Let us continue, Commander, for this will be worth it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI35
	"*The Empire of the Rising Sun has the most unique build system in that our structures are all created from special units called Nano-Cores."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI36
	"*Cores may \"unfurl\" at the location of your choosing, much like an MCV unpacks into a Construction Yard. However: unfurled Imperial structures cannot pack back up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI37
	"*Go into your Production Structures queue and build a Generator Core."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI38
	"*The Generator Core will be yours to control as soon as it emerges from your Construction Yard. If you select it, you may give it move commands around the map like any unit."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI39
	"*To unfurl it into an Instant Generator, while having it selected, use its Unfurl special ability, much like you did with the MCV earlier in this lesson."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI40
	"*You should now have a ghosted image of the Instant Generator attached to your cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI41
	"*Select a spot on open terrain to make your Generator Core unfurl at that location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI42
	"*All Nano-Core are amphibious, so they can cross land as well as water. This means the Empire of the Rising Sun can spread its borders far and wide."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI43
	"*The Imperial Docks is the only structure that cannot unfurl on land, while the Mecha Bay and Instant Dojo cannot unfurl at sea."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI44
	"*One last thing about Imperial production structures: They must be upgraded individually to unlock new construction options. You'll find these upgrades in their build queues."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT02_TSUNAMI45
	"*Now, Commander, do you see how superior our production capability is compared with that of my barbaric friends here?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN01
	"*Why hello again, Commander! In this lesson, you're gonna get acquainted with your units and some of the abilities that make them unique."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN02
	"*Every unit in Red Alert 3 has some sort of special ability, in addition to its primary ability. The majority of your units' primary abilities is to attack their targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN03
	"*A unit's special ability may put a nasty status effect on an enemy, switch to an alternate weapon, or even transform into an entirely different unit."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN04
	"*Oh, so that's how it is, then?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN05
	"*As stated earlier, not all special abilities need to be targeted like the Cryocopter's Shrink Beam. Some abilities cause units to switch weapon modes."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN06
	"*Blimey, that tank looks like he's lost control! And all you've got is an Allied Hydrofoil!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN07
	"*Its primary weapon is an anti-air cannon that won't do you any good here. However, if you use its special ability, it'll switch from its gun to the Weapon Jammer."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN08
	"*Select the Hydrofoil now and ready the Weapon Jammer by left-clicking on its special ability button or hitting the F key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN09
	"*Select the Hydrofoil now and ready the Weapon Jammer by selecting it in the Command Menu, or pressing the X button while holding the Right Bumper."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN10
	"*Proper."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN11
	"*Now, have your Hydrofoil fire on that Soviet Apocalypse Tank on the shore."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN12
	"*Hah! So much for that tea party."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN13
	"*As you can see, the Apocalypse Tank can no longer fire. Not so scary now, is 'e?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN14
	"*So remember: Even the toughest enemy units may be vulnerable to your lesser units' special abilities. Learn them all, and never give up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN15
	"*No robots are gonna get past you, Commander!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN16
	"*You should know, there are some units at your disposal whose primary ability either isn't a weapon at all, or will change depending on what you tell it to attack."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN17
	"*For example, each faction has its own type of Engineer unit, like this swarthy fellow over here."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN18
	"*Engineers are special units that can capture any enemy structure or neutral tech structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN19
	"*Much like with moving or attacking, you can select your Engineer and right-click on a capturable structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN21
	"*That'll make him go after it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN22
	"*Look, there seems to be an Oil Derrick you can capture out in the water. Oil Derricks are neutral tech structures that provide additional income."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN23
	"*Go get it!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN24
	"*Off he goes! Note that Engineers are amphibious, so they automatically switch to a keen aquatic form when they get to water. Not all units are amphibious of course."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN25
	"*Notice you can issue capture commands into the fog of war. Assuming the structure is still there when you get to it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN26
	"*You may have noticed that when you highlighted that enemy structure with your Engineer selected, your cursor changed to a garrison cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN27
	"*That garrison cursor indicates a structure you can enter."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN28
	"*Your basic infantry can't garrison enemy structures or neutral tech structures like the Engineer can, but they can garrison civilian structures such as hotels and houses."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN29
	"*When infantry garrison these structures, they receive extra protection as the building they're in will take damage instead of the units themselves, should they come under fire."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN30
	"*Garrisoning your units into civilian structures is both a good tactic both from an offensive and defensive perspective."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN31
	"*It helps to secure locations, force enemies to take an alternate path, or give your units more cover near to your base should the enemy send a force to destroy you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN32
	"*Now garrison that nearby structure by issuing a move order onto it whilst having some Peacekeepers selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN33
	"*Good, they're in. And here comes trouble."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN34
	"*As you can see, those enemy training robots fired upon the structure rather than directly at your Peacekeepers."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN35
	"*Watch out, though, because each faction has ways of clearing out garrisoned structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN36
	"*Now, let's say you need to get your Peacekeepers out of the structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN37
	"*Just select the structure and use the Evacuate command, just like using a special ability on a unit."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN38
	"*Do this now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN39
	"*Some of your units can also be garrisoned by your infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN40
	"*The Multigunner IFV is a unique Allied vehicle whose weapon takes on the characteristics of whichever infantry unit hops inside."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN41
	"*Order one of your Peacekeepers into that IFV and watch what happens."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN42
	"*Other units, such as our Allied Spies like this one here, also have contextual attacks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN43
	"*Select the Spy, then use his contextual attack on one of those enemy training dummies."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN44
	"*Hahaha, now who's the dummy, am I right?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN45
	"*As you can see, the Spy's primary ability is to disguise himself as the enemy."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN46
	"*Alternatively, if you highlight an enemy structure, you can try to infiltrate it to disrupt the enemy's base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_GUARDIAN47
	"*C'mon, lads, we have to get through this. Commander, that's the end of this lesson. See you in the next one."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER01
	"*Wait, what...? No way, not me again!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER02
	"*Aaah, I'm melting!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER03
	"*Hey... Where did that Engineer go, anyway...?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER04
	"*Ow!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER05
	"*Fear not, for civilians have long since abandoned such structures once they heard we were coming."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER06
	"*The Allies and Empire can try rushing their Peacekeepers or Imperial Warriors into a garrisoned structure, while the Soviet Conscripts can use their Molotov cocktails."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER07
	"*...If I may?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER08
	"*Normally the IFV's weapon works best against aircraft.  But once you garrisoned your Peacekeeper into it, it changed to an anti-infantry weapon."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER09
	"*While the IFV can only contain one infantry unit at a time, other vehicles can hold more, and can transport your infantry around the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER10
	"*For example, the Riptide ACV is admittedly a good transport for getting infantry quickly and safely from one point to another, although infantry cannot fire out of it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER11
	"*Garrison your remaining infantry into the Riptide now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER12
	"*Now that they're garrisoned, let's move your Riptide across this lake and over to the shore on the other side."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER13
	"*Look for the marker on the Radar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER14
	"*Riptides are a special type of unit in that they're amphibious, meaning they can traverse both land and water."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER15
	"*As my comrade said, not all units are amphibious, so it's good to make note of the ones that are."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER16
	"*Some units behave differently on land and water. For instance, when your Riptide is on water, its torpedo tubes open to give it additional firepower."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER17
	"*Now that you've made it to the other side, let's get those Peacekeepers out."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER18
	"*All transports have the not-so-special ability to evacuate their passengers. Use the Evacuate ability now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER19
	"*By the way, try pressing the directional pad in any direction to snap your cursor to the closest unselected target in that direction. This is useful for pinpointing targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_HAMMER20
	"*Ooh…but why?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI01
	"*Let us go over how to use special abilities now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI02
	"*Select that Allied Cryocopter, if you please."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI03
	"*The Cryocopter's special ability is the Shrink Beam."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI04
	"*With the Cryocopter selected, left-click on its special ability button in the bottom right of your screen, or press the F key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI05
	"*Notice that the Shrink Beam is a targeted special ability, which means you have to left-click on a target to use it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI08
	"*Other types of special abilities take effect as soon as you press the ability button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI09
	"*Now then, use the Shrink Beam on my good friend the Soviet Hammer Tank."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI10
	"*Betrayed! After all we've been through!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI11
	"*If you're finished with your motivational speech, perhaps we can continue?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI12
	"*Commander, let's go over a unit whose special ability is... to transform!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI13
	"*One basic example is the MCV, though let us take a look at a more-exciting case in one of the Empire of the Rising Sun's versatile Mecha Tengu units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI14
	"*The Mecha Tengu is an amphibious hovering anti-infantry unit that can transform into the Jet Tengu, a flying air-superiority fighter."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI15
	"*Not only does the transform ability affect how it navigates the battlefield, it also means the unit changes from having anti-ground weapons to anti-air weapons."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI16
	"*Select the Mecha Tengu and use its special ability."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI17
	"*Impressive, no? Now... order your Jet Tengu to destroy that miserable Cryocopter!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI18
	"*Oh, and don't worry -- it is merely a training robot carefully disguised to look like a real vehicle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI19
	"*He went into the structure, you fool! And there he shall remain, forever! For that is the Way of the Engineer."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI20
	"*Of course, you could just blow the structures up if you cannot be bothered by such details."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI21
	"*Finally, let us discuss Contextual Attacks. A Contextual Attack is what you get when your cursor changes to something other than a normal attack cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI22
	"*Select the Allied commando who has showed up so very unexpectedly."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI23
	"*This \"Agent Tanya\" has different ways of attacking targets, depending on the type of target."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI24
	"*When you order her to attack enemy infantry, such as these lifelike robots, your cursor will be that of a normal attack cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI25
	"*However, when you highlight an enemy vehicle or structure, you get a demolition cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI26
	"*When ordered to demolish a target, Tanya will move very close to the target, set some charges, and blow it up. This is an example of a contextual attack."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI27
	"*Go ahead and dispose of those forces using the commando."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI28
	"*Infiltration has different effects depending on which type of structure is infiltrated. Experiment with all the possibilities."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT03_TSUNAMI29
	"*Incidentally, the Empire of the Rising Sun's Shinobi unit may also infiltrate structures. Only the tactless Soviets lack an infiltrator."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN01
	"*Why hello, hello, Commander!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN02
	"*In this particular lesson, we're going to be covering Top-Secret Protocols and how to use them, as well as the Threat Meter and some other heavy stuff."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN03
	"*To begin with, let's have a look at this here base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN04
	"*Let's say you're low on credits. If at any point you decide that you no longer want a structure that you’ve placed, you may sell it!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN05
	"*To sell a structure, left-click on the Sell button under your Radar, then left-click on the structure you wish to sell. Right-clicking cancels out of Sell mode."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN07
	"*Try selling one of those Power Plants now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN08
	"*Relax, friend, I was just about to explain to the Commander here how to repair. \nIt's pretty important."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN09
	"*To repair a damaged structure, left-click on the repair button under your radar. Then left click on your Construction Yard."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN11
	"*Give it a go."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN12
	"*Now then, let’s talk about Top-Secret Protocols."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN13
	"*Now let's go over how to access your Protocols."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN14
	"*Left-click the Top-Secret Protocols button, or press the Tilde hotkey to the left of the 1 key, to bring up a menu of all the dirty tricks you can use."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN15
	"*Open the Command Menu and drill down to your Support Powers in the 6 o'clock position. Then select the Top-Secret Protocols button in the center."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN16
	"*As you can see, this menu has, what, like 15 different Protocols to choose from."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN17
	"*The Protocols are ranked by levels, so to access Protocols further down the list, you need to access the ones above them first."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN18
	"*For example, you can't get Cryoshot until you get Surveillance Sweep."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN19
	"*Each Protocol costs one Security Point."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN20
	"*Now, go get Surveillance Sweep from your Top-Secret Protocols menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN21
	"*Well well, sir, looks like you've been cleared to use Surveillance Sweep! What an occasion!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN22
	"*All protocols available to you will appear on the left-hand side of your screen."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN23
	"*To use Surveillance Sweep, first left-click on it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN24
	"*To use Surveillance Sweep, open the Command Menu, drill down to your Support Powers, and select it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN25
	"*Now you need to select a target location for the sweep."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN26
	"*This one's a little dodgy because you then have to select a second location to plot a trajectory."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN27
	"*So left-click once, then again someplace else in the area near the edge of the screen."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN29
	"*Give it a go."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN30
	"*See that? Make sure to have a look at the notes written next to each Protocol so you're aware of what you're signing up for before you pick one of these."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN31
	"*By the way, the Protocols available to you are determined solely by the faction you're commanding."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN32
	"*So even if you pull a stunt like capturing an enemy ConYard, doesn't mean their top brass will open the kimono on their military secrets. Makes sense, yeah?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN33
	"*Watch how one of your units gains veterancy by mowing down droves of hostile targets."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN34
	"*Heroic forces like these can make a huge difference, so best keep 'em around."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN35
	"*Speaking of which...what's all the commotion over there?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN36
	"*Oh-hohoho, now it's on!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN37
	"*Try to build up enough forces to stop your enemy's invasion, then take those units to the enemy's base and destroy it!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN38
	"*Take note as you build units that your Command Point total keeps increasing. This represents the total sum of units you can have in the field at one time."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN39
	"*Smashing work, commander. You're now one step closer to becoming a serious threat out there."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_GUARDIAN40
	"*We're done with this lesson. See you in the next one, all right."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER01
	"*He was a good Power Plant... but you can build another."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER02
	"*Don't go crazy selling everything. What would your friends think if you failed a tutorial mission?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER03
	"*Hey--! Quit it!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER04
	"*You'll notice that a repair icon has appeared on your Construction Yard, indicating that it's undergoing repairs."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER05
	"*Structures can only repair as long as you have sufficient funds. You may notice that as your structure is repairing, your credits are slowly trickling down."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER06
	"*Top-Secret Protocols is just a fancy term for special support powers you can use. These will affect the battlefield, your enemies, and your units and structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER07
	"*Basically, they can get you out of a pinch."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER08
	"*Keep in mind, you need your Construction Yard intact in order to use them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER09
	"*As mentioned earlier, there are different types of Protocols."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER10
	"*There are offense-oriented protocols such as Surgical Strike, which can damage enemy forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER11
	"*There are more-tactical protocols such as Chrono Rift, which can protect your units or split enemy forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER12
	"*And then there are upgrade protocols that provide passive bonuses, such as Advanced Aeronautics, which toughens up all those weak little Allied aircraft."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER13
	"*Unlike offensive and tactical protocols, upgrade protocols take effect immediately once acquired and do not need to be activated manually."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER14
	"*Next we'll talk about the Threat Meter, which gives you an impression of how much death and destruction is happening all around you in a given moment."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER15
	"*The Threat Meter increases in battle, especially when you sustain heavy casualties, and the higher it is, the faster you earn new Security Points."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER16
	"*Higher levels of threat also influence how quickly your units gain combat veterancy. The higher the threat, the faster your units will become great heroes from killing foes!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER17
	"*Veteran units display a little chevron. They're better at killing enemies, and once they achieve Heroic status, they automatically regenerate to boot."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER18
	"*Remember, you also have access to your Top Secret Protocols to help you take down your enemy!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_HAMMER19
	"*Ow!! Whatever, figure out yourself then!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI01
	"*Each faction has its own set of Protocols, which can be offensive or defensive in nature--sometimes both."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI02
	"*As you progress through a battle, you'll gradually earn Security Points, which you can use to access new Protocols."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI03
	"*Progress towards your next Security Point is indicated by the meter surrounding the Top-Secret Protocols button on your screen."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI04
	"*The number in the button is your current number of Security Points."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI05
	"*Progress towards your next Security Point is indicated by a special meter next to your Radar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI06
	"*The number beside the meter is your current number of Security Points."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI07
	"*It appears you are under attack. Take advantage of your high threat meter and vet up your forces while using some of your Top-Secret Protocols to assist you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT04_TSUNAMI08
	"*Fear not, for this is only a simulation involving lifelike robots."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN01
	"*Back for more, then, Commander? In this particular lesson, we’ll be going over some of the more-advanced play mechanics that'll separate the men from the boys."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN02
	"*From earlier lessons, you should be aware of the Allied Spy and some of his capabilities by now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN03
	"*Spies can disguise themselves as enemy units. Only scout units--the Allied Attack Dog, Soviet War Bear, and Imperial Burst Drone--can detect disguised enemy units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN04
	"*Spies and Imperial Shinobi can also infiltrate enemy structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN05
	"*When you infiltrate a structure, it'll impair your enemy's base in various ways, which should give you the upper hand."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN06
	"*For example, if you infiltrate their enemy Reactor, the entire base will power down for a while."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN07
	"*Go ahead and infiltrate the Instant Generator by right clicking on in it whilst your Spy is selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN09
	"*Good job, sir. Your units made it back and were able to whittle down those enemy tanks' health enough for your base defenses to finish them off."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN10
	"*Had you issued a normal move order back to your base, your Guardian Tanks might not have fared as well."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN11
	"*Incidentally, should the enemy catch you off guard with an attack, listen for audio cues from your Intel Officer and visual cues on Radar to tip you off."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN12
	"*To jump to the most recent Radar event, just hit the Space Bar."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN13
	"*Or to get back to your main base from anywhere in battle, tap the H key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN16
	"*Ah, pants. It looks like the Empire is sending another attack wave, but this time they've come at us with infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN17
	"*Your base defenses are strong against infantry, but with that many of the blighters, I don't think it's going to be enough."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN18
	"*So, a good way to dispatch large quantities of infantry is to crush them with vehicles."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN19
	"*Not all vehicles can crush infantry so it's good to familiarize yourself with the ones that can."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN20
	"*Small vehicles like your IFVs and Riptides are examples of vehicles that can't crush."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN21
	"*On the other hand, larger vehicles like Guardian Tanks and Assault Destroyers can crush a man like so many potato crisps!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN22
	"*What's more, some of the largest vehicles in Red Alert 3 are big enough to crush other, smaller vehicles."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN23
	"*Anyhow - let's crush those robots!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN24
	"*Thought you'd never ask! To crush enemy infantry, select your Guardian Tanks and issue a move order behind the enemy infantry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN25
	"*You can also issue a Force-Move command using the G hotkey or using the Advanced Commands tab near the bottom of the screen."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN27
	"*Issue a move command to the designated location with your tanks now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN28
	"*Seeing as how that Rising Sun base seems intent on taking us down, let's go over some ways to get your units to protect your base without being drawn out by the enemy."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN29
	"*All of your units can be set to different stances, which affect their behavior."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN30
	"*All units start off in Guard Stance, meaning they will auto-acquire enemies that come within their attack range, and pursue them for a short distance if they try to flee."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN31
	"*Once the dust settles, your units will return to their original positions."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN32
	"*We need to have some of our units on defense for our base but not pursue our enemies."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN33
	"*To do this, we need to put them into Hold Ground Stance. First, select one or more of your tanks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN34
	"*Now click on the Advanced Commands panel in the bottom right of your screen next to the unit portrait."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN35
	"*As you can see, this panel reveals some additional controls for your units."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN36
	"*Now open the Command Menu and take a look at all the available stance options."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN37
	"*Select the Hold Ground button to change your units' stance."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN38
	"*Perfect. What say we also set up some base defenses? Each faction has a couple of its own base defenses. The Allies have Multigunner Turrets, for example."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN39
	"*Select the Support Structures tab in the Sidebar, build a Multigunner Turret, and place it near your tanks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN40
	"*Open the Command Menu, navigate to your Support Structures queue, and build a Multigunner Turret. Then place it near your tanks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN41
	"*Multigunner Turrets change weapons if you put different infantry into them, though the rocket launchers they use by default should be handy in most cases."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN42
	"*I've been meaning to tell you, by the way: If you have units selected and you open the Command Menu, you can back up to the top level just by pushing the B button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN43
	"*You don't need to deselect anybody."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN44
	"*Then, if you want to get back to your selected units, drill down to the Current Selection button located in the 7 o'clock position in the Command Menu,"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN45
	"*Capital. Now if the Rising Sun attacks, we'll have some extra defenses waiting for them that they won't be able to draw away from out base. And here they come!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN46
	"*As you can see, they've decided to retreat back to base, but your Guardian Tanks stood their ground and didn't continue after them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN47
	"*Had your Guardian Tanks followed them back, they most likely would have been destroyed by the Empire's own base defenses."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN48
	"*Well, good job, Commander. You now know some of the advanced tactics that'll surely make you a worthy adversary on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN49
	"*And would you believe it? There are still more advanced tactics and commands for you to learn. Just dig into the options screen for a complete command list."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_GUARDIAN50
	"*But do that on your own time. This lesson's over, and there's only one more left. We're heading over to it now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER01
	"*Excellent, Commander! By infiltrating their Generator, you've brought down their entire base's power, which in turn powered down their base defenses."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER02
	"*That will certainly make it easier to destroy their base! Stupid robots!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER03
	"*Oh no! It appears the Empire of the Rising Sun is sending in a force to destroy your tanks. You'll need to retreat your tanks back to your base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER04
	"*A clever way of doing that is to Reverse-Move them back to your base. This will allow them to continue attacking those enemy units while retreating to a safer location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER05
	"*To Reverse-Move your units, select them and press the D key on your keyboard."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER06
	"*Notice how your cursor changed. Right-click on the target destination near your Construction Yard to order your tanks to retreat."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER08
	"*Another benefit of Reverse-Moving is that it keeps a unit's stronger front armor facing the enemy."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER09
	"*Most vehicles are more vulnerable from the rear and flanks, so when you retreat from enemies using a normal move command, you'll turn tail and take more damage."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER10
	"*Reverse-moving allows you units' stronger front armor to take the brunt of the fire."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER11
	"*Ew...."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER12
	"*Simple as that, you've just changed your units' stance."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER13
	"*Keep in mind that no matter what stance your units are in, any orders you issue will always be followed."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER14
	"*Stances will only affect how units behave when not under your direct control."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER15
	"*Now, take three Guardian Tanks, not counting our field-instructor, and move one to each of the designated locations and put them into Hold Ground stance."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER16
	"*You can also build walls from your Support Structures queue. To do so, build and place one wall segment, then build and place another along the same row as the first."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER17
	"*You'll see the build grid show green to indicate where you can form a solid wall. Careful, though. Each wall segment costs you, so longer walls are more expensive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER18
	"*Walls are useful for blocking smaller forces, like those pesky Engineers always trying to steal your structures."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER19
	"*Go on and try building a solid wall at the front of your base."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_HAMMER20
	"*Ow! What was that for?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK01
	"*Wait."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK02
	"*You may wish to assign your tanks to a Control Group first. This is an important way of managing your forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK03
	"*To assign units to a Control Group, select them, then hold the Control key and press a number key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK05
	"*Do this now, please."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK06
	"*Good."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK07
	"*You may now select those units at any time by pressing the corresponding number key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK08
	"*You can also jump to the group by double-tapping the key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK09
	"*You may now select those units at any time just by tapping the X button while holding the Left Bumper."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK10
	"*You can also jump to the group, or anything you have selected, by pressing the Y button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK11
	"*One further note about control groups: All units are placed into Control Groups automatically."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK12
	"*To access these, open the Command Menu, and select Control Groups in the 8 o'clock position. There you will always be able to select any of your units by type."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK13
	"*Now... please proceed with crushing my robots."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK14
	"*Yes, the Empire's base defenses are quite impressive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK15
	"*You may need to use combined arms to defeat them. In fact, if you depend overmuch on just one or two types of units, you are bound to fail."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK16
	"*Thankfully, it is easy to manage multiple types of units at once."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK17
	"*Try selecting all your combat forces on the battlefield using the Q key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK18
	"*One tap of Q selects all units onscreen. Two taps selects all units on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK19
	"*Good. Notice you have multiple unit types in the contextual tab in your Sidebar at right."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK20
	"*One type of unit in your group will always be selected. To cycle between unit types, simply tap the Tab hotkey. Try this now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK21
	"*Yes, that's it. You may also cycle unit types in reverse order by pressing the Tab key while holding the Shift key."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK22
	"*Try selecting all your combat forces on the battlefield by double-tapping the X button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK23
	"*Good. Notice that when you open the Command Menu, you have multiple unit types selected."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK26
	"*You may navigate to different unit types in the Command Menu to use their special abilities or change their stances."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK27
	"*Or, without opening the Command Menu, simply hold the Right Bumper while tapping up or down on the D-pad to cycle between unit types."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK28
	"*Switching unit types in this fashion makes it easier to use your mixed group's special abilities, without deselecting the group."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK29
	"*We should also briefly touch on Waypoint Mode, for it's useful. Waypoint Mode lets you queue up move or attack orders."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK30
	"*To use Waypoint Mode, hold the Alt key while issuing move or attack orders as normal with units selected. Your units will complete the orders in sequence."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK32
	"*Now, earlier we had mentioned how directional armor comes into play during battles."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK33
	"*Another type of armor bonus your units can receive comes from an automatic reaction to enemy fire called suppression."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK34
	"*Suppression only affects infantry units. When infantry units become suppressed, they go prone on the ground and continue firing."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK35
	"*Suppressed infantry are slower but more resistant to damage."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK36
	"*Send your infantry into that city square there and attack that garrisoned structure."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK37
	"*Banzi! As you approached the structure, your units came under enemy fire and some of them were suppressed as a result of the enemy attacks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK38
	"*Due to this suppressed position, your units could absorb more damage and in turn deal more damage to that enemy structure, allowing them to destroy it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT05_TSUNAMITANK39
	"*That... was for my robots...!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_COOLEG01
	"*My work here is done, my friend. I'll see you on the other side, where the real action is!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN01
	"*Finally, the last lesson! Feels good to be almost finished, eh Commander? Let's get started."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN02
	"*In this lesson, you'll learn how to work with your Co-Commander to help achieve victory on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN03
	"*You'll be working with a Co-Commander throughout the campaigns in Red Alert 3."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN04
	"*You can fight alongside a friend, or if you don't have any friends, the game will provide one for you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN05
	"*No matter which campaign you're playing, your Co-Commander's forces will always be green."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN06
	"*No matter which campaign you're playing, your Co-Commander's forces will always be gold."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN07
	"*In general, you can expect your Co-Commander to do a halfway-decent job of fending for him- or herself or helping you out."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN08
	"*But just in case, we've set up a handy-dandy interface for you to issue specific directives to your partner."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN09
	"*In the upper left hand of your screen is the Co-Commander Monitor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN10
	"*Unfortunately this won't let you control your real friends, but it's useful when fighting alongside one of the game's Co-Commanders."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN11
	"*Now, the next directive is Strike Target. This directive makes your Co-Commander immediately send available forces to destroy that target, and anything nearby."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN12
	"*Much like last time, to issue a Strike Target directive you must first select the button. Then move your cursor over an enemy and left click on it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN13
	"*Much like last time, to issue a Strike Target directive you must hold the Left Bumper, then tap right on the D-pad. Then select a target with button A."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN14
	"*Issue a Strike Target directive on that enemy Boot Camp."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN15
	"*See that? Your Co-Commander's always got your back, Commander!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN16
	"*Lastly, let's go over the Keep Command directive. This one makes your Co-Commander fend for him- or herself, and he or she will always do so by default."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN17
	"*Unlike the other directives, this one does not require you to select a target, and may be used to cancel the other directives."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN18
	"*To issue this directive, simply select the Keep Command button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN19
	"*To issue the Keep Command directive, hold the Left Bumper and tap down on the D-Pad."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN20
	"*Try this now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN21
	"*To give your Co-Commander the signal to execute the Strike, select it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN22
	"*To give your Co-Commander the signal to execute the Strike, select it and open the Command Menu."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN23
	"*This brings up a window explaining the strike. To confirm the tactic, select the Execute button."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN24
	"*Go ahead and give your Co-Commander the signal now."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN25
	"*You may also choose to cancel a Co-Commander Strike that's already in progress."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN26
	"*On that note, great job, Commander.  You now have the know-how to work with your Co-Commander."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN27
	"*As you can see, your Co-Commander can help you do some of the heavy lifting."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN28
	"*Now get out there, and knock some heads together!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN29
	"*Go on, what are you waiting for, a fancy ending with a sappy montage?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_GUARDIAN30
	"*As for you, boys...? The truce is off!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER01
	"*Now let's go over all the functions."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER02
	"*First and foremost, there's a handsome image of your Co-Commander to remind you who you're fighting alongside."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER03
	"*For this tutorial you'll be fighting alongside the fresh-faced Soviet Commander Oleg."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER04
	"*Right next to his portrait are the various directives you can issue. Basically, you can boss him around."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER05
	"*The first is Take Position, which causes your Co-Commander to immediately send his available forces to a target location."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER06
	"*To issue this directive, select the Take Position button. Then move your cursor over the battlefield and left-click again in a target area."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER07
	"*To issue this directive, hold the Left Bumper and tap Left on the D-Pad. Then move your cursor over the battlefield and press the A button in the target area."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER08
	"*Go ahead, please."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER09
	"*Good. Notice how Oleg promptly responded by sending his forces to the position you requested."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER10
	"*Alternatively, you may open the Command Menu and drill down to the Communicator, located in the 9 o'clock position. Here you will find the different directives available."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER11
	"*That is how we do it in Russia! Notice how Oleg immediately responded with his forces."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER12
	"*Another option is to use the Plan Attack directive."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER13
	"*This directive makes your Co-Commander build a good-sized force to eliminate any enemy units in the target area, as well as any enemies encountered along the way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER14
	"*As with the others, to issue a Plan Attack directive, just select the button, then select a target enemy or location on the battlefield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER15
	"*As with the others, to issue a Plan Attack directive, hold down the Left Bumper and tap Up on the D-pad. Then select a target area using button A."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER16
	"*Go ahead and use Plan Attack on the other side of that valley."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_HAMMER17
	"*Finally!! You jerks!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_TSUNAMI01
	"*Now then. We have one final type of directive to review."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_TSUNAMI02
	"*During the course of some missions, you will come across what we call Co-Commander Strikes. These are situational tactics your co-commander will use when given the signal."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_TSUNAMI03
	"*Notice how one has just appeared on the battlefield. Co-Commander Strikes may appear anywhere, anytime during a mission, and it's yours to decide how best to use them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_TSUNAMI04
	"*Let us examine that Co-Commander Strike more closely."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MT06_TSUNAMI05
	"*Shut up!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA01
	"Turn back, Yuriko![1.2]You're going to get hurt."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA02
	"I can't believe it.[1.4]You're stronger than I thought possible."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA03
	"Troops, seize the girl, put her back in her cell."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA04
	"She's more powerful than we thought possible."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA05
	"Send in the Steel Ronin!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA06
	"Send additional troops to lock her down."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA07
	"Unpack the defenses; halt her progress!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA08
	"We're not trying to hurt you, Yuriko,[2]but you must stop!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA09
	"Be careful with her you buffoons.[1.8]I said contain her, don't kill her!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA10
	"You've killed her!  Our experiments have only begun!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA11
	"You've killed her!  We'll have to start all over!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_DRSHIMADA12
	"Don't shoot her when she's shielded you idiots![2.4]You're killing yourselves."
