	"She's there."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IMPERIALSOLDIER31
	"Target incoming."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI01
	"You must get more powerful so you have a chance of fighting them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI02
	"You're more than they can handle now.[2.3]Find me and help me!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI03
	"Take out their barracks."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI04
	"Discover yourself: Find all the Secret Files."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI05
	"You can now shield yourself; it will reflect their weapons back at them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI06
	"Yes, keep yourself safe."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI07
	"Their minds are weak; you can lure them over to fight for you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI08
	"Yes.  Now they will be your cover."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI09
	"You can slam enemies and objects.  Tear this place apart!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI10
	"You can lift and slam enemies and objects.  Use it to unblock your way."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI11
	"Yes, soon you will be free!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI12
	"You can improve yourself: become faster, stronger, or tougher."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI13
	"Another improvement awaits."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI14
	"You're reaching the limits of your power."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI15
	"Use the computer."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI16
	"Yuriko, rise.  You're going to break free from this place."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI17
	"Yuriko, wake up.  Break free and find me!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI18
	"Yuriko!  Don't give up!  Find me."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_IZUMI19
	"Yuriko!  Come back for me!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO01
	"Where am I?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO02
	"I need to access the data terminal."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO03
	"I should use my Psychokinetic Burst."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO04
	"I'm injured...I need to find a trauma station."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO05
	"I need to find a way to clear away all that junk."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO06
	"I need to find a way to get that door open."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO07
	"I can juggle those Steel Ronins.[1.9]They're not as tough as they look."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO08
	"I can use Psychic Domination on those soldiers."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO09
	"My Psionic Shield should protect me from those vehicles."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO10
	"These heavy doors are resistant to my powers."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO11
	"Why are they shooting at me then? "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO12
	"No, please!  Don’t do this."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO13
	"First I lift them, then I throw them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO14
	"I can't hold my Psionic Shield for long, but it can bounce back enemy fire while it's up."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO15
	"I can only dominate a few soldiers at a time."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO16
	"Each time I learn from one of the data terminals, my power grows stronger."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO17
	"I've unlocked all my latent Psionic Talents. Good."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO18
	"Now, I just need to get out of here!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO19
	"Now, I just need to find Izumi!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO20
	"Don’t worry, sister. I’m coming."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO21
	"I sense that was the last of the data terminals here."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO22
	"So this is one of Dr. Shimada's data terminals.[3.1]Nothing but dirty pictures and Mahjong games."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO23
	"Six of my captors died after teasing me last year.[3.6]That must be when I first learned my psychokinetic burst."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO24
	"Once I mastered the Psychic Domination talent, everyone in this facility started being much nicer to me."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO25
	"They trained me to move heavy objects with my mind.[3.5]There are dozens of accident reports blamed on my so-called Psionic Slam."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO26
	"This is test data from my Psionic Shield training.[3.3]If they didn't expect I could reflect live ammunition back at them, they shouldn't have shot at me."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO27
	"Each time I learn about myself from one of these data terminals, I regain some of the power that my captors have been trying to suppress."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY01_YURIKO28
	"This place used to be a medical facility, so its trauma stations are second-to-none.[4.5]If they manage to hurt me, I should seek one out."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER01
	"Containment area breached! Sound the alarm!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER02
	"We've got a high-priority threat! Battle stations!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER03
	"Containment area compromised!  All available troops to containment area one!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER04
	"It's no use, retreat!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER05
	"She's too strong! Fall back!!!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER06
	"What is she?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER07
	"She's in the perimeter!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER08
	"Oh my god!  Run!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER09
	"She's just a girl, what is this?!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER10
	"She's broken into other holding cells."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_ALLIEDSOLDIER11
	"Target is on the move."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_IMPERIALSOLDIER01
	"We've got you![1.1]Don't struggle- we have you surrounded.[3.3]On order of the Emperor, you are under arrest."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_IMPERIALSOLDIER02
	"What's happened?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_IMPERIALSOLDIER03
	"This doesn't look like Pearl Harbor…"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_IZUMI01
	"It is time to wake up, Yuriko."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_IZUMI02
	"Please come back and rescue me. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_IZUMI03
	"Destroy them Yuriko!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_IZUMI04
	"After what they did to you, they have no right to live."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_IZUMI05
	"Feel the power smolder inside of you! Let it all out!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_IZUMI06
	"Hurry my sister! The Allies are rallying against you!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_SOVIETSOLDIER01
	"How do I get home from here?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_SOVIETSOLDIER02
	"This was colder than Siberian Tundra!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_SOVIETSOLDIER03
	"Is the war over?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO01
	"I should find all the Secret Files in this base.[2.4]I might discover their weaknesses."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO02
	"Izumi, my sister, I have failed you.  I'm sorry."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO03
	"And now I leave this place.  "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO04
	"My head... I'll need some time before my Psionic Talents come back to me."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO05
	"They kept me here like an animal...[2]I'll just have to bring this whole place to the ground."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO06
	"Hmm. I wonder what would happen if I opened the cells?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO07
	"I should destroy all the factories so they can’t hold anyone else."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO08
	"I should dominate a few engineers and make them repair that bridge."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO09
	"Those lasers hit hard. I need to use my Psionic Shield."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO10
	"Is that one of the Soviets' Desolator Troopers? He might come in useful."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO11
	"The Allies can't hide their secrets from me.[2.5]I should find all their data terminals here before I destroy this place."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO12
	"Those Aircraft Carriers are the last things standing between me and Shimada."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO13
	"Shimada can wait; I am going to tear this place apart first."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO14
	"I should free all the prisoners... They know what it's like..."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO15
	"I’ve destroyed everything of value here, I should get to the port."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO16
	"I'm finished here. It's time I returned to the Empire of the Rising Sun.[4.1]I've got a score to settle."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO17
	"How long was I kept here?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO18
	"I need to think my way out this cryo prison."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO19
	"Those rocks…aren’t really rocks. Damn the Allies."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO20
	"That Desolator Trooper, they haven't even figured out how to remove his suit without killing him. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO21
	"Something about a new bombardment system called the Pacifier.[3.6]FutureTech pitched it to the Allies as an alternative to their orbital defense network."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO22
	"A log of all the Soviet prisoners of war stationed here, who surrendered after the battle of Leningrad.[5.9]How shameful."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO23
	"This base recently received a huge shipment of Cryo Cannisters from FutureTech.[5.3]I guess it helps keep the prisoners on ice…"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO24
	"They're calling this a \"VIP containment center\" because they freeze their subjects rather than just lock them up?[6]This is just a prison camp."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO25
	"The Allies have commissioned hundreds of Cryo Legionnaires from FutureTech to help 'keep the peace.'"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO26
	"They've been testing some new aircraft called the Harbinger.[3.2]They stuffed an entire proton collider inside of it."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO27
	"Wait, so most of these guys are just FutureTech's hired guns?[4.1]The Allies are just buying their military muscle now?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO28
	"This is a list of the commanders responsible for the attack on Tokyo Harbor.[4.4]They're being hailed as heroes..."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO29
	"Allied propaganda demonizing the Crown Prince Tatsu.[3.5]If not for the Prince, I might never have been born...[6.4]For better or worse."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY02_YURIKO30
	"One day, I'll be free to make my own choices.[2.7]Not be at the whim of some strange cursor."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_DRSHIMADA01
	"I've blown the elevator, Yuriko.[2]You'll never find your way down to me."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_DRSHIMADA02
	"Another elevator has collapsed.  Give up!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_DRSHIMADA03
	"I don't understand why you're being so persistent."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_DRSHIMADA04
	"Yuriko, I made you.  I don't want to hurt you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_DRSHIMADA05
	"You're going too far, Yuriko."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_DRSHIMADA06
	"Attention Imperial Troops: you are fully authorized to kill Yuriko."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_DRSHIMADA07
	"Reinforcements!  Someone help!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_DRSHIMADA08
	"No, you're making a mistake!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_DRSHIMADA09
	"Please! I can protect you."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER01
	"The cloning area is overrun."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER02
	"Activate the clones!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER03
	"Weapons lab!  Get to the weapons lab!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER04
	"Rocket Angels are on-site."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER05
	"Air support flying in!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER06
	"King Oni brigade detached."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER07
	"Giga-fortress rise!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER08
	"Archer Maidens: move-in."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER09
	"Warriors, swarm her!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER10
	"Psychic inhibitors are online."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER11
	"Psychic inhibitors are offline."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER12
	"We're in a lot of trouble here."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER13
	"She's back! "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER14
	"Everyone run for your lives!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER15
	"Please don't kill me!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER16
	"We can't stop her! She's too powerful!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IMPERIALSOLDIER17
	"It wasn't me.  I never touched you!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI01
	"There are other access points, Yuriko.[2]Find them!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI02
	"He won't seal himself in, seek out the last elevator."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI03
	"Find a way down!  "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI04
	"We are almost united, Yuriko."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI05
	"Yuriko, locate the elevator down to Shimada's private lab."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI06
	"Get me out of here, Yuriko."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI07
	"You were always Shimada's favorite!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI08
	"I will kill you!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI09
	"You're the last thing in my way!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI10
	"You freed me.   Now allow me to release you!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI11
	"You're dead!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_IZUMI12
	"You are…quite powerful. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO01
	"Those psychic inhibitors are preventing me from using my powers."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO02
	"I need to find the elevator down."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO03
	"He’s blown up the elevator…[1.4]I need to find another one."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO04
	"Hmph. He did it again... there must be another elevator."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO05
	"Shimada... This is getting tiresome."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO06
	"There's no use in hiding."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO07
	"Watch them run!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO08
	"Is that all you’ve got?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO09
	"I need to free Izumi."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO10
	"I need to kill Izumi. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO11
	"I have to double back. They'll be waiting."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO12
	"Good, more fools for the slaughter. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO13
	"I need to push the debris aside."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO14
	"Izumi, I'm coming!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO15
	"Izumi, you're free!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO16
	"Shimada! I’ll kill you! And bring down this entire facility!"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO17
	"What are you doing? "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO18
	"After all I’ve done for you! "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO19
	"I’ve been through hell to find you. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO20
	"You’re as good as dead. Give it up. "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO21
	"What happens now? "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO22
	"What do I do now? "
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO23
	"A detachment of Imperial Archer Maidens volunteered to provide extra security here in exchange for psychic training."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO24
	"They seem surprised by how resistant I've become to physical harm and to physical pain.[4.9]Apparently they've taken quite an interest in trying to find my breaking point."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO25
	"What a disgrace.[1.4]Those Steel Ronin were just a bunch of common thugs and murderers with an exceptional violent streak."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO26
	"It seems they've invested in Psychic Inhibitors this time around to try and dampen my psionic talents.[6.2]We'll see how that goes for them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO27
	"So these are my sisters, my own flesh and blood.[3.5]I would have expected it to feel better than this, knowing I had family.[7.8]But I feel nothing for them."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO28
	"Looks like an old invoice concerning the damage I caused the last time I was here.[4.6]So many billions of yen...[6.8]But still they dared to rebuild this place."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO29
	"Izumi's old report cards...[2.3]Survivability, A-plus average.[4.8]Focus, B-plus average.[7]Discipline, A-minus average.[8.8]Power, S-average."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO30
	"This is a laundry list...[1.8]Literally.[2.8]What do these people need with 2,000 plaid skirts?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO31
	"They're keeping dozens of military-grade nanocores down here, even though this place has no official military connections."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO32
	"A profile of Dr. Gregor Zelinsky, considered to be an expert in relativity and physics, and a complete nut-job. How do he and Dr. Shimada know each other...?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO33
	"A list of donors to this facility and an invitation to some sort of banquet.[4.8]Now how come I didn't get an invitation?"
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO34
	"A whole bunch of military-grade gear from this place went missing in the Sakhalin islands. Someone's gonna be in trouble."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO35
	"This must be the trauma center,[1.9]I bet I can fill it with bodies."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO36
	"Such fear lingers here.[2]This must have been Izumi’s cell."
End

DIALOGEVENT:MY03_YURIKO37
	"This must be where they do the cloning.[2.3]There could be…hundreds of me."
End

DIALOGEVENT:SHINZOSPEAKS
	"[0.8:3.1]Do not struggle, warrior child. You cannot win.[4.5:3.9]I have never seen somebody so small, yet so destructive![8.8:2]But you will learn obedience.[11.3:-491.8]You will learn."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN02DESC
	"Units in Red Alert 3 each have a unique special ability. How effectively you use these will decide the outcome of your battles! To quickly use the selected unit's ability, just hit the \"F\" hotkey."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN03DESC
	"Scouting is essential to victory. Try quickly training up a scout unit and take it to the enemy's base to see what he's got in store for you. Then create the appropriate counters, and have at it!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN04DESC
	"Remember to purchase and use your Top-Secret Protocols, which are special powers that can get you out of a pinch or turn the tide of battle. To get new powers, click the button in the lower-left corner of the screen!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN05DESC
	"Get more income by expanding to as many Ore Mines as you can! In general, you should place an Ore Refinery in the spot right in front of an Ore Mine, and you only need one Ore Collector per Mine."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN06DESC
	"Capture those Neutral Tech Structures! An Oil Derrick boosts your cash flow, Observation Posts reveal the surrounding fog of war, and more! These structures can swing the battle in your favor."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN07DESC
	"Go navy! An amphibious or pure-naval strategy can catch your opponent by surprise, while giving you free reign over vast portions of the battlefield."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN08DESC
	"Terror Drones got you in a tizzy? Simply drive your infected vehicles back to one of your vehicle production structures (or the Soviet Crusher Crane) and their repair drones will fix you right up!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN09DESC
	"The Empire of the Rising Sun upgrades its production structures individually, by researching Nanotech Upgrade and Nanotech Breakthrough, respectively. These unlock new construction options in a structure."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN10DESC
	"Defend your Ore Collectors at all costs! They may crush enemy infantry as a last resort, and some have unique defensive abilities. If you do lose a Collector, you can build another from your Refinery."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN13DESC
	"Beware of Spies! The Allies' Spy unit may disguise himself as any other infantry. Sniff him out with your faction's scout unit, before he gets close enough to cause any trouble!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN14DESC
	"The Soviet Hammer Tank features the devious Leech-Beam special ability, which can siphon enemy armor and even weapons! Once you've stolen a weapon, switch back to primary firing mode for twice the punch!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN15DESC
	"The Allied Spy and the Imperial Shinobi may infiltrate enemy structures, causing all sorts of bad things to happen to their foes. The consequences of infiltration depend on which type of structure is infiltrated."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN16DESC
	"CRYOCOPTER - The Allies' incredible Cryocopter may freeze enemy surface units, rendering them immobile and extremely vulnerable to attack! Cryocopters may also shrink units down to embarrasing, crushable proportions!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN17DESC
	"CENTURY BOMBER - The Allies' sturdy heavy bomber can pound enemy structures into dust in a carpet-bombing run, then paradrop infantry units behind enemy lines so they can finish off anything left standing."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN18DESC
	"VINDICATOR - The Allies' close-support sortie bomber is perfect for swooping in to put a serious dent into enemy armor divisions. Should it come under anti-aircraft fire, it can autopilot back to base in a snap."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN19DESC
	"MIRAGE TANK - The Allies' high-tech Mirage Tank is the ultimate anti-tank assassin. Its spectrum cannon can tear through armor, and it camouflages itself while still. Plus its special ability makes nearby units invisible!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN20DESC
	"APOCALYPSE TANK - The heaviest tank ever made. As if this monstrosity's twin cannons were not enough, its magnetic harpoon can prevent faster foes from escaping its destructive attacks."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN21DESC
	"TSUNAMI TANK - The mainline Imperial tank is uniquely capable of traversing both land and sea. Its fast-firing main gun can punch through any armor soon enough, and its special ability infuses the vehicle with a significant defensive boost."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN22DESC
	"SEA-WING - The Sea-Wing is a submersible unit that can take down enemy aircraft in a flurry of missiles. The latest model can convert to the flying Sky-Wing form, which is effective at assaulting enemy infantry from above."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN23DESC
	"The Empire of the Rising Sun's anti-air options revolve around its new Archer Maiden divisions as well as its transforming forces. Try switching to the secondary modes of your Defender-VX base defense or Mecha Tengu to take down those aircraft!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN24DESC
	"The Allies must advance their tech at each of their expansion bases independently. Research Heightened Clearance to unlock the second tier of units, then get up to Max Clearance for the mightiest forces of all!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN25DESC
	"Submersible units such as the Soviets' Akula Sub are invulnerable to most attacks and invisible to enemy Radar while under water! However, they must surface in order to attack their targets."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN26DESC
	"Remember Reverse-Move! You can make certain units move in reverse by using the \"D\" hotkey. This lets you continue firing on an enemy target while drawing him into your carefully-laid traps!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN27DESC
	"Have you tried building your base exclusively on water? If you're up against an opponent who relies too heavily on ground forces, get out to sea and mount an amphibious assault!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN28DESC
	"Make sure your base is fully powered at all times! Keeping your power levels in the green keeps your base defenses online and your production structures cranking away at full speed!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN29DESC
	"The Soviet Super-Reactor can solve all your power needs! Just don't let your enemies blow it up or it's liable to destroy half your base. Try selling this structure before it explodes!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN30DESC
	"The frontline infantry unit on each faction can counter enemy units garrisoned in buildings! Peacekeepers and Imperial Warriors just need to get inside, while Conscripts can toss their Molotov cocktails."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN31DESC
	"BURST DRONE - Imperial Burst Drones can latch onto and slow down your vehicles and aircraft, and even self-destruct to deal damage! Shoot them down using anti-air units, or by targeting any vehicles they've attached themselves to."
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN32DESC
	"If the enemy is attempting to capture your Construction Yard with an Engineer, you can always pack up into an MCV to thwart his sneaky strategy! Then crush the Engineer and experience sweet revenge!"
End

ECS:BETALOADSCREEN33DESC
	"TESLA TROOPER - Not even a tank can crush the Soviet Tesla Trooper, who can obliterate most targets with his electrifying attack. His special ability is to switch on an EM disruption field, which disables enemy vehicles nearby."
End

ECS:ENGAGINGCONTENTDESC
	"The battle is about to commence. Battlefield control interface coming online. Construction Yard uplink imminent. Good luck, commander."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDAPOLLODESC
	"APOLLO FIGHTER - The Allies' Apollo Fighter is one of the fastest, most reliable air superiority fighters in the world. Its twin autocannons can shred enemy aircraft, and it can quickly return to base if threatened by anti-aircraft fire."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDASSAULTDESTROYERDESC
	"ASSAULT DESTROYER - The Allies' state-of-the-art amphibious warship features a powerful swivel-mounted main gun as well as the unique Black Hole Armor, which draws enemy firepower in the vicinity. Now that's taking one for the team!"
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDCHRONOSPHERE2DESC
	"In recent years, the Allies have managed to withstand the Soviet onslaught using various unorthodox new weapons and technologies, such as the Chronosphere. Much of this equipment was jointly developed by the Allied Nations, in partnership with advanced defense research firms such as FutureTech."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDCHRONOSPHEREDESC
	"The Allies recently unlocked the secrets of matter-transport technology in the Chronosphere, one of many cutting-edge engineering marvels developed in secret by the minds at FutureTech. The Chronosphere offers nearly limitless tactical possibilities to the shrewd battlefield commander."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDEVADESC
	"LIEUTENANT EVA McKENNA - Eva was the best student in her academy classes year after year, and now personally attends to the highest-ranking members of Allied coalition, ensuring a strong chain of command. Affected by the Soviet-Allied conflict from a young age, she has dedicated her life to serving the Allied cause."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENALLIEDPROTOAPOLLODESC
	"Because the Allied Nations are linked by a common enemy and ideology rather than by national borders, it is little wonder that they possess one of the finest air forces in the world. Necessity forced the Allies to rapidly prototype their aircraft designs into today's highly-efficient models."
End

ECS:LoadScreenAllies
	"Having defeated the Soviet Union's leaders and disarmed the Empire of the Rising Sun, the Allies still faced difficult problems on two fronts, even though the war was officially over. Pockets of revolutionaries in both the Union and the Empire continued to require military intervention, even as tensions between the two defeated nations simmered to dangerous new levels."
End

ECS:LoadScreenCryoLegionnaire
	"CRYO LEGIONNAIRE - When Allied peacekeepers could no longer contain the riots following the Imperial invasion, FutureTech Corp. saw the opportunity to field-test its Cryo Legionnaires, whose cryo-cannons could freeze the seething throngs dead in their tracks, without causing permanent harm."
End

ECS:LoadScreenDasha
	"INFORMATION OFFICER DASHA FEDOROVICH - By taking advantage of her technical status as a civilian, Dasha managed to avoid the same fate as most of the Soviet leadership once the Allies took Leningrad. Afterwards, she immediately began working to reconnect with other survivors and patriots, in her determination to ensure the Union's sovereignty and to restore its strength."
End

ECS:LoadScreenDesolator
	"DESOLATOR TROOPER - There is a saying in Russia that mistakes are made only when they are admitted, and for once, its notorious Ministry of Experimental Science made a mistake when it introduced the Desolator Troopers. Their poisons are so vile that other Soviet forces soon learned to stay far away."
End

ECS:LoadScreenEva
	"LIEUTENANT EVA MCKENNA - Rumors swirled once the Lieutenant took an extended leave of absence after successfully coordinating many of the war's pivotal battles, though she returned to work four months later, as composed and dedicated as ever. Her colleagues all say she is an indispensable part of the Allies' communication network."
End

ECS:LoadScreenFutureTank
	"FUTURETANK X-1 - FutureTech Corp. silenced critics of its \"FutureTank\" program with the unveiling of its X-1 prototype, a robotic tank guided by an advanced AI. FutureTech claims that these vehicles will revolutionize armed conflict and prevent unnecessary loss of life on the battlefield."
End

ECS:LoadScreenFutureTechLabs
	"FUTURETECH CORP. - Some say the Allies never would have won the war if not for Amsterdam-based FutureTech Corporation, a defense contractor whose state-of-the-art military products and services are vaunted and feared all over the world."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP01
	"All commanders are advised to keep their bases fully powered at all times. Without enough power structures, your units and structures will build more slowly and your base defenses will cease functioning."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP02
	"Use combined arms to achieve victory! A well-balanced combat group includes an assortment of anti-infantry, anti-vehicle, and anti-aircraft forces. Avoid relying too heavily on any one type of unit to prevent your enemies from easily countering your armies."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP03
	"If your Construction Yard comes under heavy fire from enemy vehicles, it is advisable to escape to the waters (or onto land, as the case may be). Mobile Construction Vehicles are amphibious, and although they have no weapons, they are large enough to crush most enemies under their treads."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP04
	"Bombardment vehicles excel at taking down enemy base defenses. Should your enemy hunker down using advanced base defenses, roll in artillery to destroy them from long range! Better yet, take out the enemy's power structures to cause all those base defenses to shut down."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP05
	"Fortress Walls, available in the Support Structures queue, can be used to slow enemy troop movements and prevent enemy Engineers, Infiltrators, and Commandos from getting into your structures."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP06
	"If an enemy unit seems invincible, chances are there's a better way to fight it. Even the biggest, toughest combat vehicle has its weaknesses, and large groups of foes are all the more vulnerable to area-of-effect attacks. Mix up your tactics and keep the enemy guessing!"
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP07
	"Your forces will not automatically attack enemy structures by default, in case you want to capture or infiltrate those structures. If you plan on laying waste to the enemy's base, try switching your forces to Aggressive Stance, or use the Assault-Move command."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP08
	"Seasoned commanders agree: In battle, it's best to keep spending one's credits without exceeding one's income. This way you'll be building new military forces and additional structures at a good clip. Don't get caught sitting on thousands of credits with no army to defend them!"
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGENERALTIP09
	"If a strategy is ineffective, immediately discontinue its use! Avoid relying too heavily on any one tactic, lest your opponents catch on and bring the right counters. Keeping your enemies guessing is the key to victory."
End

ECS:LoadScreenGigaFortressSea
	"GIGA-FORTRESS - None save a scarce few highest-ranking Imperial leaders knew of the development of the Giga-Fortress, a massive, self-aware weapons platform. Fewer still fathom the destructive potential of its Gods' Breath device."
End

ECS:LoadScreenGigaFortressSky
	"GIGA-FORTRESS - Even as the Empire pressed its assault on the Soviet Union, its brightest scientific minds put the finishing touches on a highly-advanced, artificially-intelligent military computer. And in the unlikely event of the assault's failure, they vowed to awaken it and give it their lives."
End

ECS:LoadScreenGiles
	"COMMANDER GILES PRICE - After the Allied occupation of the Empire of the Rising Sun, Giles inserted himself into more and more important matters of policy, and emerged as an outspoken diplomatic leader in the world community. And yet his fighter squadrons always remain at the ready in case the Allies' old enemies refuse to go quietly."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENGILESDESC
	"COMMANDER GILES PRICE - This one-time fighter ace happily accepted a desk job since it put so many more shiny chevrons on his lapel. Now he's quickly making a name for himself as a capable, cool-headed tactician. He oversees one of the Allies' finest strategic air bases in Europe."
End

ECS:LoadScreenGrinder
	"GRINDER - As the Union continued scrapping millions and millions of tons of broken-down military equipment, the idea for the Grinder was born. Although it hasn't so much as a single gun barrel, and is notorious for its poor handling and flimsy rear armor, the Grinder can tear through anything it touches. "
End

ECS:LoadScreenHarbinger
	"HARBINGER GUNSHIP - Built for \"clean-sweep\" operations, these massive aircraft are probably the most controversial of all of FutureTech's military unveilings, partly because FutureTech owns and profits from the privatized flight schools whose pilots seem all too eager to get behind the yokes of these beasts."
End

ECS:LoadScreenHill
	"COMMANDER DOUGLAS HILL - A former war hero who volunteered to come out of retirement in order to train the next generation of Allied peacekeepers and to help establish tough policies for a post-war Empire of the Rising Sun. While some military pundits claim Commander Hill is past his prime, none who have seen his tank platoons in action share this point of view."
End

ECS:LoadScreenIzumi
	"IZUMI - Although the evidence is inconclusive, a young woman code-named Izumi is believed to be the top-ranking survivor of the Tokyo-based Shiro Psychic Research Center's secretive Omega Program--an exploration into the combat capabilities of human mind. Izumi's real name, background, and whereabouts are all unknown, as the Shiro Psychic Research Center now lies gutted and deserted."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANEXPANSIONDESC
	"The Empire of the Rising Sun may expand to unclaimed Ore Mines quickly using its Refinery Cores. Imperial Ore Collectors even possess a special defensive weapon for use against enemies that dare threaten resourcing operations."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANMECHAKINGDESC
	"SHOGUN EXECUTIONER - Unrivaled, Prince Tatsu's near-unstoppable creation has cut a path through the Soviet countryside. Now its six eyes are set squarely on the Union's capital city. Its mission has been hard-coded: Moscow and the Kremlin must be utterly destroyed, the Soviets' time-machine along with them."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANNAVYDESC
	"The Imperial navy is as versatile as it is deadly, often taking the Empire's enemies by surprise using amphibious assaults or long-range bombardment. Consider the seas unsafe when the Rising Sun's afoot."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANSHINOBIDESC
	"SHINOBI - These hooded assassin-saboteurs are responsible for gathering intelligence for the Empire of the Rising Sun, as well as for putting its most-hated enemies to the sword. While the Imperial Shinobi are armed only with archaic, old-fashioned weapons, they have proven to be uncommonly lethal."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANSHOGUNDESC
	"SHOGUN BATTLESHIP - The largest, most powerful members of the Empire of the Rising Sun's naval armadas are armed with six main gun batteries that can shatter even the most heavily-fortified enemy compounds from great range. To helm such a vessel is one of the Empire's highest honors."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANSUKIDESC
	"LOGISTICAL OFFICER SUKI TOYAMA - One of the most trusted officers of the Empire of the Rising Sun, Suki is a childhood friend of Prince Tatsu and was born to serve an important post within the Imperial military hierarchy. She is responsible for relaying military intelligence to Imperial commanders, and is authorized to speak directly to the Emperor himself."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANTATSUDESC
	"CROWN PRINCE TATSU - The Emperor Yoshiro's only son, and the visionary behind the Empire of the Rising Sun's unprecedented military technology. Less traditional than his father yet just as driven, Prince Tatsu is widely considered a brilliant and pragmatic leader seeking to modernize and strengthen the Empire."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENJAPANYOSHIRODESC
	"EMPEROR YOSHIRO - The longtime ruler of the Empire of the Rising Sun, cherished as a living god by his people. Emperor Yoshiro is a traditionalist who strictly follows the code of bushido, the samurai way of the warrior. He fundamentally believes that the Rising Sun’s destiny is to rule the entire world."
End

ECS:LoadScreenKelly
	"KELLY WEAVER - As the Head of Corporate Communications for FutureTech Corporation, Ms. Weaver is the ubiquitous voice of one of the world's leading private defense firms. Due to the proprietary nature of the firm's research and the highly-sensitive details of its contract with the Allies' military, she approaches her public-speaking responsibilities with utmost seriousness."
End

ECS:LoadScreenKenji
	"COMMANDER KENJI TENZAI - The Empire’s defeat was a wake-up call for Kenji, who refused to give in and redoubled efforts to complete development of new military forces intended for the ultimate defense of the Imperial homeland. And as these weapons came online, a famous smirk reappeared on his lips and the swagger returned to his step."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENKENJIDESC
	"COMMANDER KENJI TENZAI - This extremely confident officer is famous for his way with sophisticated technology and, at least in his mind, many other reasons. Kenji was put in charge of field-testing the Empire's newest fighting forces by Prince Tatsu himself, and likely has his affluent family to thank for it."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENLISSETTEDESC
	"COMMANDER LISSETTE HANLEY - As a former spy serving the Allied Special Forces, Lissette has deep insight into enemy strategies, as well as a one-of-a-kind knowledge of the Allies' most-sophisticated weapons. Her casual, almost-playful manner hints at years of experience in tense combat situations."
End

ECS:LoadScreenLydia
	"COMMANDER LYDIA WINTERS - Ms. Winters is considered to be the architect of the Allied orbital defense network, which was essential to the Allies’ victory in the last war. Having earned the right to take on new responsibilities, she pursued an opportunity to lead Allied forces directly, rather than keep watch from behind the curtain as before."
End

ECS:LoadScreenMortarCycle
	"MORTAR CYCLE - Even the messenger-bikes once used for delivering telegrams, cakes, and toiletries were subsumed by the Soviet War Machine as fighting intensified. Once reinforced with light armor plating, aftermarket engines and handlebars, and light artillery weapons in the sidecar, these bikes proved to be very effective at fast assault."
End

ECS:LoadScreenMoskvin
	"COMMANDER NIKOLAI MOSKVIN - As the Union was thrown into chaos after the battle of Leningrad, this impetuous young commander, who was previously kept on a short leash due to concerns with his psychological disposition, quietly slipped away. He has lost none of his zeal for battle and still leads a small number of seasoned soldiers, who follow out of fear or respect."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENMOSKVINDESC
	"COMMANDER NIKOLAI MOSKVIN - This intense young man quickly rose through the ranks of the Red Army's largest Tesla Trooper regiment due to his unconventional yet brutally effective tactics, and now oversees the Union's experimental forces. Some say he is psychologically unstable... but never to his face."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENNAOMIDESC
	"COMMANDER NAOMI SHIRADA - This gifted, no-nonsense fleet commander is heiress to a famous military family's legacy and is widely known to have little patience for those who get in her way of her ambitions. It is said she has no permanent home, preferring life aboard the ships in the armadas at her disposal."
End

ECS:LoadScreenOleg
	"COMMANDER OLEG VODNIK - They say this veteran tank commander was tricked into accepting a lucrative-sounding promotion to Head of Soviet Military Affairs. After all, the Soviet military was nearly annihilated in the last war, so the Soviet people hungered to lay blame at someone's feet. Despite his unenviable position, Oleg maintains an unflappable attitude."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENOLEGDESC
	"COMMANDER OLEG VODNIK - Although casualty rates among Soviet conscripts are very high, opportunities for advancement abound for those who survive the front lines. Oleg is living proof of this. In spite of his informal demeanor, he has a proven ability to lead in battle and is well-liked by most of his men."
End

ECS:LoadScreenOmegaProgram
	"THE OMEGA PROGRAM - The paramilitary firm Shiro Psychic Research secretly spent years developing an extremely ambitious system intended to augment the Empire of the Rising Sun's armed forces. Called the Omega Program, it required hundreds of human test subjects, which were brokered from orphanages, sanitariums, or wherever the unwanted gathered."
End

ECS:LoadScreenPacifier
	"PACIFIER FAV - In order to keep their rivals firmly in check, the Allies commissioned an all-terrain artillery platform with unprecedented range as well as defensive systems to protect it at close range. FutureTech Corp. obliged with the Pacifier Field Artillery Vehicle, which quickly exceeded expectations."
End

ECS:LoadScreenReaper
	"REAPER - This not-entirely-successful old prototype from the Soviet Union's Ministry of Experimental Science somehow got the green light when the Union's situation continued to worsen and most military assets turned scarce. Its scores of rockets and grenades more than make up for its deficiencies."
End

ECS:LoadScreenShimada
	"DR. SHINJI SHIMADA - As the managing director of the infamous Omega Program, Dr. Shimada is inadvertently responsible for some of the Empire of the Rising Sun's greatest weapons, such as the Psionic Decimator. He earned a Ph.D. from Tokyo's most prestigious science institute after his groundbreaking (though controversial) thesis on latent psionics and the next stage of human evolution."
End

ECS:LoadScreenShinzo
	"COMMANDER SHINZO NAGAMA - The untimely death of Emperor Yoshiro took a heavy toll on Shinzo, who was considered one of the late Emperor's most-trusted retainers. Shinzo returned to a life of seclusion at his ancestral home in Shin Iga Province, where he is believed to be searching for spiritual guidance. A less-popular theory is that he is plotting to fulfill the Emperor’s final wishes."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSHINZODESC
	"COMMANDER SHINZO NAGAMA - A calculating military leader who comes from a long line of Imperial military advisors seeking the Empire's rise to absolute power. Shinzo was one of the architects of the Imperial invasion of the Soviet Union, and has taken it upon himself to train a new generation of commanders."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETAIRFIELDDESC
	"The Soviet airforce has grown bold in recent years. Once limited to producing smaller craft, airfields are now retrofitted to manufacture everything from the sleek MiG Fighters to the massive Kirov Airships. Today, Soviet air superiority arguably rivals that of the Allied nations."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETAKULADESC
	"AKULA SUB - Invisible to enemy radar while submerged, Soviet Akula Subs lurk undersea in search of enemy ships. Although they must surface to fire, they are powerful enough to assault larger vessels directly."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETCHERDENKODESC
	"PREMIER ANATOLY CHERDENKO - Longtime leader of the Soviet Union, who has led the Union in an age of prosperity and military superiority. Once a famous theoretician, he rose to power meteorically even as Soviet forces under his advisement achieved victory after victory against their enemies the Allies."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETDASHADESC
	"INFORMATION OFFICER DASHA FEDOROVICH - Born to a poor family whose 10 children all willingly enlisted in the Soviet armed forces, Dasha was singled out as the most talented of the lot, so much so that Premier Cherdenko himself took notice of her. She now serves as an essential conduit between Soviet commanders across multiple fronts."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETIRONCURTAINDESC
	"IRON CURTAIN - The Iron Curtain is one of the Soviet military's most-feared creations. It gathers some sort of energy inside its furnace, which it uses to project a kinetic barrier onto armored forces. While the barrier lasts only a short while, affected targets are completely invulnerable during that time."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETKRUKOVDESC
	"GENERAL BORIS KRUKOV - Having fought and won countless battles against Allied forces, Krukov is a war hero in the eyes of the Soviet people. Those who know him personally, however, are more likely to be deathly afraid of getting on his bad side. He never could have achieved his status without being strict and without being ruthless."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETNATASHA01DESC
	"NATASHA VOLKOVA - Few know the true character of Natasha Volkova, the Union's legendary sniper, though her name and exploits are known across the world. A woman of few words, she is a seasoned professional--and, some would say, a cold-blooded killer. She deals with only the most urgent matters affecting the Union."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETNATASHA02DESC
	"NATASHA - So famous is this Soviet sniper-commando that her likeness is heavily used for purposes of military recruitment and propaganda. Some say she is hell-bent on living up to her living-legend image. She is extremely skilled with her custom rifle and has full authority to call airstrikes."
End

ECS:LoadScreenSoviets1
	"The Soviet Union slid into a state of deep turmoil and disorder after the Allied defeated its leaders at Leningrad. However, because the Allies were spread thin trying to demilitarize the Empire of the Rising Sun at the same time, a few brave and well-connected Soviet patriots quickly seized the opportunity to form a resistance movement, with intent to restore the Union to greatness."
End

ECS:LoadScreenSoviets2
	"In testament to the pride and determination of the Soviet spirit, the surviving forces of the Union's military soon rallied after the defeat of their corrupt leaders at Leningrad, in spite of countless losses and setbacks. Although the Soviet military now is but a shadow of its former self, some of its newest and most talented commanders are working tirelessly to carry their nation forward."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETTESLACOILDESC
	"TESLA COIL - The modern Soviet Tesla Coil is far different from the innocuous scientific device from which it takes its name. As one of the deadliest weapons developed at the Ministry of Experimental Science, this device can reduce a full-grown man to mere ash in just one tremendous electrical jolt."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETTHREEAPOCSDESC
	"The Soviets are virtually unchallenged on the ground, due to their exceptionally powerful and sturdy armor divisions. If only their Apocalypse Tanks could swim, say some Soviet political pundits, then surely the Union would have taken over all the world by now."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETZELINSKYDESC
	"DOCTOR GREGOR ZELINSKY - An ingenious and well-to-do scientist responsible for many popular Soviet household goods, a majority of which were appropriated by the Ministry of Experimental Science and eventually turned into weapons. A peaceful man by nature, Zelinsky is ambivalent about his current status as Union's top military scientist."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENSOVIETZHANA2DESC
	"Faced with a new threat in the Empire of the Rising Sun, the Soviet military's publicity department worked tirelessly to produce high-impact propaganda with which to compel millions of young men into enlisting willingly. Pictured: Commander Zhana Agonskaya, posing for a Red Air Force recruitment campaign."
End

ECS:LoadScreenSteelRonin
	"STEEL RONIN - Most Imperial soldiers found guilty of treason or war crimes are promptly executed. The most experienced ones, however, instead are locked in a sort of solitary confinement within the massive frame of a Steel Ronin assault suit. There they would lie for years in a fugue state, to be awakened for battle only in the event of the Empire's darkest hour."
End

ECS:LoadScreenTakara
	"COMMANDER TAKARA SATO - After the Allies’ victory over the Empire, the former chief of the Rocket Angels' First Battalion quickly rose to become a strong leader in the newly-founded Imperial Final Defense Force. Takara's experience in surprise assaults has made her an elusive target, and she prides herself on being an increasingly-painful thorn in the Allies' side."
End

ECS:LoadScreenTatsu
	"CROWN PRINCE TATSU - After the death of his father, the Empire's citizens feared for his only son. But rather than fall prey to desperation or despair, Prince Tatsu did something no one, not even the Allies, expected: He surrendered, and agreed to cooperate with the Allies to put an end to their war. The Imperial people perceived this surprising move as both bold and cowardly in equal measure."
End

ECS:LoadScreenThornley
	"PRES. RUPERT THORNLEY - The President of the European Union is a shrewd ambassador and businessman, who worked tirelessly behind the scenes during the last war in order to secure the necessary funding and support that eventually enabled the Allies to prevail. In the aftermath of the war, he endeavored to publicize these successes."
End

ECS:LoadScreenVera
	"COMMANDER VERA BELOVA - Known as the White Sparrow, this Ukrainian freedom fighter restored some sense of order and hope to the Soviet people after the collapse of their leadership after the war. Her promises of glory and retribution have inspired a new generation of Soviets to take up arms in the defense of their nation."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENWARRENDESC
	"COMMANDER WARREN FULLER - Not one for mincing words, Warren has survived numerous battles against the Soviets through regimented training, determination, and tenacity. Once captured by the Soviets, he fought his way to freedom with his bare hands. His men know he has a score to settle."
End

ECS:LOADSCREENZHANADESC
	"COMMANDER ZHANA AGONSKAYA - Men and women alike are conscripted into the Red Army, and Zhana distinguished herself almost immediately from among all the millions drafted as a brilliant pilot, good leader, and proud patriot. Now many of the Union's top aces seek transfer to her command."
End

ECS:STANDARDLOADSCREENTITLE
	"ESTABLISHING BATTLEFIELD CONTROL"
End

ERROR:D3DFAILUREMESSAGE
	"Please make sure you have DirectX 9.0 or higher installed. Also verify that your video card meets the minimum requirements, and that you do not have hardware acceleration disabled in the Display control panel."
End

ERROR:D3DFAILUREPROMPT
	"DirectX Error"
End

