SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_01
	"The Allies' notorious Attack Dogs are bred for battle near this training camp, run by Commander Hill, a washed-up old war hero who hasn't seen frontline battle in more than a decade. That is to say, his bark is worse than his bite. So how about we have a look at what he's up to? Just keep in mind that while he's likely to be a pushover this time around, he'll probably remember some of his old tricks when next you meet."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_02
	"In the Empire of the Rising Sun, battlefield commanders settle their disputes and trade their honor by conducting elaborate wargames, such as the one you are about to interrupt. After all, we could use a better understanding of Imperial tactics and military traditions. Together, your opponents here may pose a threat, but their tradition dictates that such duels must never be interrupted. So why not let the venerable Commander Shinzo and his wayward protégé Kenji wear each other down before you send them both packing?"
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_03
	"Commanders from each of the world powers are converging on this resource-rich archipelago in order to wrest control of the numerous Oil Derricks. They will be fighting fiercely amongst themselves, which should create the perfect opportunity for your naval forces to swoop in and finish them all. Think of the research-and-development we could green-light with all those Oil Derricks!"
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_04
	"The Rising Sun's ever-enthusiastic Commander Takara is running maintenance on one of those gigantic floating fortresses, due to a software malfunction in the targeting systems of its Wave-Force Tricannons. This is the perfect opportunity to learn more about those fortresses, as we can get some your forces onto the fortress and rig some of the Tricannons to defend your position. Even still, approaching Takara's Tricannons by land would be tantamount to suicide. Stick to long-range naval bombardment or airstrikes."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_05
	"The Imperial King Oni may not look like an obvious match for a main battle tank, but has more than proven itself in battle. Commander Kenji happens to be training a bunch of them here to smash through things with even greater efficiency. We would dearly love to understand what makes the Onis tick--we're not even sure if there's a flesh-and-blood pilot inside of those things. Why don't you spoil Kenji's little exercise so we can find out?"
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_06
	"One of our key research centers and resorts is in trouble, as two of the most reckless commanders you've fought thus far have decided to show up for a little off-the-record payback. With any luck, the joke will be on good commanders Kenji and Moskvin: You will have immediate access to all three types of construction yards and plenty of resources with which to take them on."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_07
	"More spacecraft have crashed on this island than in all science-fiction feature films combined, so we could definitely use it. We strongly advise you to keep moving while engaging the Soviet resistance movement's favorite sweetheart Vera in this particular location, since the Soviets use it to test the reliability of their satellite-decommissioning systems. In other words, watch the skies--it doesn't take our world-leading surveillance systems to know you don't want the Soviets to dump all their space-trash on top of you."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_08
	"Try to imagine, if you will, a battlefield--nay, a world--in which you had ample resources with which to build many, many tanks in order to defeat rival commanders attempting to do the same, in a grand tournament set on an island arena. Our greatest tacticians often say that the tank battle is the essence of modern warfare, and so this territory was created in order to test that theory in a very literal way. We are curious to see how you will fare."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_09
	"Commander Lydia is one of the Allies' top brains, and here she is gathering soil samples for some of her latest science experiments. You see, this territory is unusually low on ore... The implications of an ore-free world are deeply disturbing so we had best get to the bottom of this before she does. In order to avoid any setbacks, we are granting you 10 times the usual amount of credits for this operation. Best spend them wisely. As for Lydia, she is said to be less conservative than she looks. But even she cannot spend forever."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_10
	"As the Soviets, Allies, and Empire of the Rising Sun continued to wage their petty wars, quite a rivalry developed between the leading women on each side. Now each of these spirited young ladies is convinced that she is superior, and so the three of them are having it out in the middle of nowhere, with little but their pride at stake. Why not go check up on them to make sure everybody's playing fair? We're as curious as they are to see who the real winner is. Just make sure she goes home a loser like the rest of them."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_11
	"This is where many of the Allies' spies-in-training practice the arts of disguise, infiltration, bribing, swimming, smooth-talking, bowtie-tying, and more. Luckily for you, weapons training isn't part of the regimen, so if you play your cards right, it should be no trouble for you to wipe all those smug looks off of their faces. Be sure to do the same to Commander Giles, their supervising officer. We should be able to gain considerable insight into the Allies' spy network as a result of this particular operation."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_12
	"This island region is used to train Imperial Shinobi in infiltration, assassination, meditation, intimidation, evasion, succinct speech, and long-distance swimming. Unfortunately for the Empire, the Soviets happen to be testing a new waterproofing compound for its Terror Drones here as well. That means we have an invaluable opportunity here to survey both Imperial and Soviet close-quarters combat tactics. We strongly advise building plenty of fortress walls and anti-infantry defenses to keep your opponents at bay."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_13
	"Although the Imperial Commander Shinzo is seen as a stern traditionalist, his dedication to the Way of the Warrior is greater still. So he is here at his island retreat, learning the virtues of one of the Empire's most advanced vehicles, the Sea-Wing. It would be awfully nice to know exactly how its propulsion systems work, and how its pilots manage to avoid motion sickness. So why don't you go take a look for us?"
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_14
	"You've heard of Vera, right? She's the Russian top ace who's stuck having to teach a bunch of Soviet half-wits how to fly. Unfortunately for us, her squadrons located an area we find very intriguing, and wish to claim for our own. To make matters worse, the good Commander Giles dropped everything to come here once he heard Vera was in town, probably because his ego can't handle her being the better pilot. Why don't you step right in the middle of their little lovers' quarrel and take advantage of the situation?"
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_15
	"One of our secret training facilities is under attack by a wayward company of poorly-trained Soviet forces. Although they managed to surround this position, we have the high ground, and believe that their impulsive commander Moskvin will not hesitate to send his troops crashing against our defenses. We expect you will encounter no problems here."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_16
	"The Empire of the Rising Sun must be in real disarray; look no further than the animosity its commanders are showing one another here, as they squabble over which of them rightfully deserves to stay in this rather-pleasant island. How about you teach them to play nice next time? Take advantage of all the bad blood between them. We may learn a thing or two about their command structure in the process."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_17
	"Well isn't this just great. It seems Commanders Shinzo and Kenji have finally reconciled and are working together again, just like old times. It would be better if the two of them weren't quite so chummy, since their combined forces pose a significant threat. If you think you have what it takes to defeat them, then please proceed by all means--you'll find them training here. As Kenji is being groomed as Shinzo's successor, Shinzo is likely to hold back until Kenji gets into serious trouble."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_18
	"This stormy island was thought to be deserted until we traced several transmissions on an old emergency broadcast channel set up by the Allies several decades ago. Unfortunately, little could be heard beyond static before the transmissions were abruptly cut off. So we hired some locals from the nearest population center to bring back eyewitness accounts, though their reports were too ridiculous to be believed. Moreover, the Soviets and Allies tracked them here. Look...we just need you to clean up this mess, whatever it is."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_19
	"The Imperial Commander Takara has issued a formal duel, following the old traditions of the Empire of the Rising Sun, and is waiting to do battle against you here in the middle of the sea... She must like you! At any rate, she seems to know our gambit at this point, and has anted up with the Empire's own Shogun Battleship. You wouldn't want to disappoint her now, so please proceed with care. The technology found in the Shogun Battleships' cannons will be an excellent acquisition."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_20
	"It seems your recent victory over Commander Moskvin has left quite an impression on the young man. He is beginning to understand our plans, and says he is willing to ignore them, but only if you agree to fight him again on his own terms. Expect him to make ample use of his nasty little Terror Drones, and we also recently spotted Badger Bombers flying to the scene, bearing heavy payloads of desolator toxins. "
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_21
	"Get this: The Empire somehow snuck one of those Nanocores across the ocean all the way out here. Not only that, it contains plans for their biggest and most powerful stationary weapon. How about we do the locals a favor and take care of it? In so doing, we stand to learn a great deal about their unusual research into psionics. That stubborn has-been Shinzo has sworn to protect the weapon, but you should be able to make him break that promise, just as long as you can break through all his defenses."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_22
	"Well isn't this sweet. It seems the good Commanders Giles and Vera are becoming awfully friendly with one another, as they've set aside their differences after the last time you dealt with them. They're now looking to use the combined might of the Allied and Soviet air forces against you. We can't have them colluding with one another, so please go ahead and show their little planes to the ground. That ought to darken the skies over their little relationship."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_23
	"The weather is uncommonly clear way out here, so the Allies use this place for troubleshooting their orbital defense network--the very same network creating competition for our services. Supervising the job is Commander Lydia Winters, the woman largely responsible for the Allies' ability to smite from the heavens using their Athena Cannons. While the task is somewhat dangerous, by engaging the Athena Cannons here, you will buy us time enough to triangulate their satellites' locations and complete our map of the Allies' orbital array."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_24
	"Our sources indicate that a highly-classified military research initiative in this region is exploring how to augment the Empire of the Rising Sun's insignificant fighting population through the use of genetic cloning... apparently the Empire never learned its lesson after the Shiro Incident, though maybe we can learn something instead. Supposedly, you will be able to deploy an arbitrary number of our commando units here. That's the good news. The bad news is, you can expect your enemy to respond in kind."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_25
	"It seems you've finally riled up the Soviets, which may or may not be good news depending on how you look at it. Their three top commanders are hunkered down in the frozen northern reaches of the Union, which is where the helium mix for their notorious Kirov Airships is bottled and distributed. The Kirov is the crown jewel of the Soviet War Machine, so it would make quite a prize. But taking on Oleg, Moskvin, and Vera all at the same time seems ill-advised. Are you sure about this...?"
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_26
	"All right, we've got a problem. Some of the commanders you've run into before ganged up to locate one of our facilities, and now they aim to take it down in a little after-hours operation. They mean serious business this time, though we haven't confirmed whether they want payback against all of us or just you... The only good news is that your base is already established, while they're just getting started. Work quickly to take advantage of the head start. You do the job and we'll cover it up, hmm?"
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_27
	"Recently, Commander Oleg got not only a handsome new officer's cap, but the burdensome responsibility of restoring the Union to its former glory. Here he is in the middle of nowhere, trying (and failing) to improve on the heaviest Soviet battle tank. What does he think he's going to do, slap some missile launchers on it...? And yet, the Powers That Be have taken interest, so we're looking to you to send him back to the Motherland red-faced and empty-handed. Be ready to hit his armor as hard as you can."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_28
	"It is a dangerous world we live in indeed, if a man such as that Commander Giles is authorized to use the Proton Collider. Why not teach him a few safety lessons for everyone's sake? We would learn much about the Allies' superweapons program in the process. Just be careful--this place is far enough away from civilization that Giles isn't going to think twice about using that thing against you, if he has enough time to get it warmed up. Worse, it seems he may have access to more than one..."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_29
	"This remote island is used to sort and maintain the Empire of the Rising Sun's Nanocore units, and right at this moment, the self-assured Commander Kenji happens to be using them to practice some new tactics. It would be useful to know what he has in mind, exactly, so please go ahead and take a look. Whatever he's planning, expect him to heavily rely on those Nanocores here."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_30
	"The Allies' Commander Giles fancies himself to be quite the airman, and this happens to be the place where he trains his squadrons in all their annoying tactics. So how about you clip their wings? Dealing with Giles may be a bit troublesome for you, since the long stretches of terrain here are going to give those aircraft plenty of breathing room. But you've seen a few of his tricks by now. And soon we'll know them all--our ground teams will recover as many black boxes as possible once you're finished here."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_31
	"There is a secret competition held amongst top-ranking Imperial commanders in which they square off using only infantry, in a pure test of martial skill. It seems you have received an invitation to this year's event--you should feel honored, especially since you will get to fight not one but three commanders, who briefly set aside their differences for a chance to defeat you. To even the odds a bit, we've arranged for you to start with multiple Construction Yards. Good luck."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_32
	"Although surviving battles probably builds skill and character, it is ultimately a dangerous and time-consuming process. To address this, we are looking into means of implanting training \"memories\" directly into our soldiers, and the results are promising. The Allies must think so, too, as their Commander Hill has taken it upon himself to prove to his superiors that our program's subjects could never stand up to his battle-hardened veteran squads. Use our forces here to make sure his little crusade meets with resounding failure."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_33
	"We were surprised to learn that the Soviets made significant advances to their Iron Curtain technology and are now able to render an entire area indefinitely enshrouded in the Curtain's effect, with little additional power requirement. We promptly captured one of these advanced Iron Curtains, though sadly, our engineers on the inside were discovered. They knew the risks, of course, and you know the drill: Destroy Commander Oleg's forces and his Iron Curtain, so that we can commence evacuation operations."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_34
	"Your old friend Commander Hill has seen his share of explosive warzones in his day, so perhaps that explains why he opted to look after this dumping ground for unused munitions. Unfortunately for him, we need it. There's so much TNT here that you had better watch your step. Commander Hill had better do the same, assuming you can figure out how to use all those fireworks to your advantage."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_35
	"We are always looking for additional performance data on the Empire of the Rising Sun's pilot-assisted combat robots, for the sake of our own research. The Imperial Commander Kenji, one of the men responsible for the Empire's new generation of fighting forces, is training a recently-awakened platoon of Steel Ronin here. This is a rare opportunity to observe these strange battle suits in action. Supposedly the men inside the Steel Ronin are violent Imperial war criminals, sentenced to a sort of solitary confinement..."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_36
	"The Empire of the Rising Sun's Giga-Fortress may be the most advanced weapon ever developed, so we would very much like to have a look at it. And we know that you of all people must have what it takes to crack a couple of them open. Commander Takara will be waiting--she knows what we're after. You've already brought us so far. But if you can do this, our R&D will catapult a century ahead. In which case, we'll have something special for you. Come back soon."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_37
	"Commander Vera is a true-blue (true-red?) Soviet freedom fighter, who relies upon improvised weapons and tactics in order to earn some unlikely victories. Here she has discovered a stash of old Sickle prototypes, better known as Reapers, all covered in rust and grime. But she has restored them to working order quickly, and their multiple weapons appear to be very dangerous. It would be best if you could disarm her before she gets any ideas."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_38
	"There's been a terrible industrial accident here involving several Super-Reactors, a shipment of explosive barrels, a Conscript, and a Terror Drone. So of course Commander Moskvin was first on the scene so that he could try out his new Desolator Trooper divisions and make sure they truly are immune to environmental catastrophes. Although the Desolator Troopers are by all means vile, their ability to withstand extremely toxic conditions is intriguing, so it would be good of you to investigate."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_39
	"This is the complex in which the ever-resourceful Soviet military came up with the idea for the Grinder, after a construction accident involving a souped-up steamroller resulted in eight deaths, 37 injuries, and several million rubles' worth of property damage.  The ever-delicate Commander Oleg is here putting the Grinders through the paces. Historical data shows that he isn't going to give them up without a fight."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_40
	"A scheduled service update in our central cryosystems has caused one of the Allies' orbital cryo satellites to become unstable. Their commanding officer in this region is none too pleased, for we have arranged for her to be held accountable for this problem. Expect to face the full brunt of our cryo-capable weaponry here. We must ensure this never happens again."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_41
	"After you gave Commander Hill his first thrashing in more than a decade, he started practicing again, getting back to what he considers \"tip-top shape.\" He wants a rematch, and who are we to deny such a thing to such a kindly old man? More importantly, the Powers That Be want to see how you fare against him and one of our latest designs. They suspect it might be too advanced for someone like him. Perhaps you think you can handle it, though...?"
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_42
	"Commander Giles seemed a little distressed after you abruptly ended his partnership with Commander Vera, so now he is off sulking in Central America, trying to act important from behind a desk. We didn't mean to push him out of the fight altogether, so why don't you provoke him into another little scuffle? Besides, it will give you an opportunity to square off against one of the new mercenary squadrons working for the Allies in the area. Defeat them and one of our finest new aircraft will be yours."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_43
	"This place is often used for testing of some of the world's deadliest and costliest weapons. Due to all the demand, such weapons come fast and cheap here, so you had best make good use of them quickly. Commander Oleg is already on the scene, trying to wrap his thick head around some of the Soviets' own special weapons. Why not run him out of town? It's best not to have to share an area such as this."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_44
	"This was the site of a particularly fierce battle in which the Soviet Union's infamous Natasha wound up shooting the pilots out of dozens of different vehicles. And now, Commander Vera is trying to clean up the mess, while her rival Takara threatens to snatch up as many operational vehicles as possible. Do not wait for them to settle in. Get your forces to those vehicles as quickly as you can, and drive Vera and Takara out. There's a treasure trove of forensic evidence waiting for us here."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_45
	"The temperamental young Moskvin has taken over a strange old castle in the middle of nowhere and is using it to conduct all kinds of twisted military experiments. As the son of a late Soviet experimental technology minister, Moskvin's knowledge and tactics are valuable to us, so we need you to go ahead and engage him. Unfortunately this place is too close to the Soviet heartland so we're going to fly in under the radar. Or not fly at all, to be exact. You'll have to make do without air support."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_46
	"In her spare time, your bespectacled friend Commander Lydia enjoys attempting to improve upon the homogenous residual-interactive neutron kinetic (or \"S.H.R.I.N.K.\") technology found in the Allied Cryocopter. Unfortunately, this goes against the end-user licensing agreement dictating that the technology must not be reverse-engineered under any circumstances, and her experiments are already creating some irritating problems. We would appreciate it if you taught her a lesson in reading the fine print."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_47
	"Commanders Shinzo and Hill have fought on nearly a dozen occasions in the past, and even now they're prepare to have at it again, out in the middle of the Pacific. So get ready to get wet; we rarely have the opportunity to examine the Imperial and Allied navies in such a pristine, controlled environment. Because those two are carrying an old grudge, they'll surely direct most of their pent-up aggression towards each other. Just be ready to clean up after them."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_48
	"The Allies are working on some key advancements to the Chronosphere tech they've come to rely on, and you're going to have a look at what they're up to. Make sure their research suffers some unfortunate setbacks while you're at it, though be careful--Commander Lydia is here, and after the last time you dealt with her, supposedly she's been real keen to have another go against you. Don't expect her to go as quietly this time, and mind that Chronosphere of hers..."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_49
	"The Soviets' latest, careless attempt to meddle with new military technology is code-named URSA MAJOR, and we need you to put an end to it here before the program reaches fruition. This program is the pet project of that oaf Commander Oleg, who will be a nuisance if you do not take care of him quickly, along with whatever this URSA MAJOR thing is. Best to proceed with caution..."
End

SCENARIO:DESCRIPTION_50
	"Sorry to break this to you, but we don't expect you to succeed here. Please don't take it personally. Nevertheless, you are cordially invited to square off against all three of the Allies' commanders, who have worked out a strategy that they say you will never be able to defeat; and we believe the threat is credible. For what it's worth, in the unlikely event of your victory, our finest prototype will be yours."
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_01
	"DEAD MEAT"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_02
	"BLOOD FEUD"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_03
	"OFFSHORE KILLING"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_04
	"ALL GUNS BLAZING"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_05
	"GOSH DARN MONGOLIANS!"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_06
	"SUPERB COMMANDER"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_07
	"WHERE SATELLITES GO TO DIE"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_08
	"NO MATCH FOR THE GUARDIAN"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_09
	"YOUR GOLD MINE HAS COLLAPSED"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_10
	"CAT FIGHT"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_11
	"NO PLACE TO HIDE"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_12
	"ROBOTS AND NINJAS"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_13
	"TWO SIDES TO EVERYTHING"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_14
	"CAUGHT IN THE CROSSFIRE"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_15
	"DEFENSE OF THE ARCHIPELAGO"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_16
	"BATTLE ROYALE"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_17
	"SHOW OF FORCE"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_18
	"KING OF THE MONSTERS"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_19
	"HIGH SEAS DUEL"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_20
	"DIRTY TRICKS"
End

SCENARIO:TITLE_21
	"COME AND GET IT"
